    97	
    98	**6. The worker's flow**
    99	
   100	1. Read the brief; write the need in one line: medium, platform and ratio, subject class, goal, cast constraint, inputs available.
   101	2. Open INDEX.md, pick one or two shelves, read only their index files.
   102	3. Per variant choose one base and up to three modifiers; drop any pair listed in conflicts; drop any variant whose scene_class is review or whose cast breaks rule g at B43.md:17 unless the brief records the client's request.
   103	4. Compose three variants one axis apart; prefer higher rank, and put one draft or low-ranked shortcut in the third so the library learns.
   104	5. Generate native drafts on the studio's current default engine; never upscale before his eye.
   105	6. Build the contact sheet with ffmpeg, shortcut names under each frame, and bring it to him.
   106	7. On his click append feedback rows; the approved output enters KUTUPHANE.tsv on his word and is proposed as a new shortcut when it carries a new recipe.
   107	
   108	**7. Delivery and the board**
   109	
   110	Building sessions run install.sh; the battery runs its check. Employees get a tested-only bundle tagged by date, registered in `library_items` as kind plugin, name kisayol, version the tag; the Media Studio department's grant goes through `control_library_action`, which he clicks. The seat then receives the Skill tool and a Read confined to the bundle, as `packages/orchestrator/src/worker-shim.ts:444` already does for granted plugins. No raw row reaches an employee; the bundle is the holding's own text, so B41's customs path holds.
   111	
   112	Board: the B43 hub router consumes the forms; B64's studio master calls the skill; B28 winners and B84 needs enter as drafts through the same intake; B12 owns sound, video shortcuts carry none; B42 reads the form labels; B33 queues local samples once built, until then samples run by hand; C29 shows one group with children once a screen exists; B32 means no screen now; C41 personas point at the skill and hold no prompts. Order: the plan is registered in B43.md now; skill and library are built at B43's rank after the reorder.
   113	
   114	**8. Ordered steps and verification**
   115	
   116	1. Register the plan as an adaptation inside B43.md. Verify: only that file changes.
   117	2. Freeze raw hashes. Verify: sha256sum output in the row.
   118	3. Curation scripts, lexicons, fixture tests. Verify: tests pass, output lexicon hits 0, counts printed.
   119	4. Skeleton: SKILL.md, taxonomy, lint, index builder, three seed shortcuts. Verify: lint exit 0, index equals files.
   120	5. Shelf slices by parallel helper-writers. Verify: lint, spot-read, parity.
   121	6. Core sampling and contact sheets. Verify: native-size files, one per form.
   122	7. His eye. Verify: feedback rows; status flips only by script; until then every shortcut carries the UNVERIFIED label.
   123	8. Install, typecheck, battery, Sol pass. Verify: IDENTICAL on check, battery green.
   124	9. Release bundle, registry row and grant in the construction engine. Verify: SELECT shows the row, the bundle test passes, a granted seat lists the Skill.
   125	
   126	**9. Risks**
   127	
   128	- Keyword categories are guesses; step 4 shelves by hand and measures a sample.
   129	- Popularity is not ad quality; grade and recency outrank cluster size, and cutting SD tag-soup wholesale loses some good rows.
   130	- Brand or person leakage past lexicon, review and lint; the residue is named in the row.
   131	- Safe parts can compose a forbidden whole; conflicts, scene_class and the drop rule guard it.
   132	- Prompts tuned to Seedance or nano-banana may not transfer; re-sample on engine change through B42.
   133	- His eye is the bottleneck; contact sheets batch verdicts.
   134	- No local reference-edit model; edit-type shortcuts sample only through Codex or a paid engine.
   135	
   136	**10. His decisions**
   137	
   138	1. Money: none for the first release; sampling runs on the Codex tool and the local H3 lane. Recommend no spend now; paid engines arrive with the B43 hub.
   139	2. Content: drop every raw row hitting the forbidden lexicon with no exception list; keep woman-presenter shortcuts flagged client-request and never a default pick; video shortcuts carry no music. Recommend yes to all three.
   140	3. Scope: drafts visible to building sessions, tested only to employees. Recommend yes.
   141	4. Order: may the curation, helpers only and no money, run before the board reorder while the skill build waits its rank? Recommend yes; it sorts, it does not build.
   142	5. The creator's 45 DM shortcuts need an outward account step. Recommend skip; we build our own and the five named are covered.

