    29	// construction's settings files and plugin manifests (none applied), listed the repository with rg
    30	// from its working directory, and wrote ~/.claude.json and its peer-registry entry under
    31	// ~/.claude/sessions/. With CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, an empty working folder (PWD matching it) and
    32	// XDG_CACHE_HOME of its own, the login, the global config, the peer registry and the MCP debug log
    33	// all live in the company home, and nothing of the repository is listed. The same membership — his
    34	// one login in that home; a home without it answers "Not logged in" and never falls back to ~/.claude.
    35	// Sol's single pass on phase 3 refuted the first shape: the env was the parent's minus CLAUDE*, so every
    36	// other path-moving variable followed the call in (GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=<repo>/.claude/…/SKILL.md reached
    37	// the file); the home check took the repository, a relative value and links out of work/ or cache/;
    38	// and the construction's own folders were derived from $HOME. Now the env is an ALLOWLIST (COMPANY_ENV
    39	// below) and HOME is the company home too — so the CLI's built-in look-ups (~/.claude/ide,
    40	// ~/.config/anthropic, rg's ~/.config/git/ignore), the residue phase 3 first had to name, fall inside
    41	// it; the home is absolute, canonical, outside both the construction's ~/.claude and the repository,
    42	// and its parts stay inside it; the construction's folders come from the passwd entry (os.userInfo()).
    43	//
    44	// The tools a seat holds are still the compiled gateway profile (R2.2), passed explicitly.
    45	// `DXB_WORKER_ISOLATION=0` is the rollback shape (the pre-2026-09-05 behaviour).
    46	export interface SdkIsolation {
    47	  settingSources: never[];
    48	  settings: { autoMemoryEnabled: false };
    49	  persistSession: false;
    50	  strictMcpConfig: true;
    51	  cwd: string;
    52	  env: Record<string, string>;
