straint; the seats stay at xhigh; `budget_minutes` per seat on the call sheet → `due_at` along the dependency chain in `queue_dispatch`'s one transaction (an unbudgeted seat keeps the 7-day default; the record says `all`/`some`/`none`); `queue_sheet_times`, the read-only times table per seat and per sheet with the non-engine/engine ratio (1.18 on 005's own book) and one English line per seat for the verdict; an idle lane's rest 10 s → 3 s (`DXB_LANE_REST_SECONDS`; `10` rolls back); one line in the Creative Director's §3 (v9); a seat is never told its minutes — the number lives in the book (his word: the per-seat estimate stays as approved). Battery: tsc clean · b43 45/45 · 171 neighbours green · i18n PASS · pinned in 22/22 profiles · scheduler restarted 21:50:00. Not built by the approval's wording: the gauge on the studio tab (B32). Evidence: `EVIDENCE-clock-2026-09-13.md`. **His eye is given — 2026-09-16 <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b43-road-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 -->; what it still owes is its first measurement on the next film through the road.** **(3) CONTINUITY BETWEEN SHOTS — PARKED 2026-09-14 with the rule he accepted (*"ok"*, with his scope on Flux) <!-- CEO-OK: astra-rule-accepted-flux-scoped-to-local-2026-09-14 -->:** every film he has accepted is ONE prompt, ONE take, ≤ 15 s (the station's limit 15.1 s); the "4 kusur" of C66 came from cutting a film into four locked shots; continuity inside a take is the prompt's, between takes it is unproven here and failed the one time it was tried. GPT-6 Astra, asked on his order (`COUNSEL-gpt-6-astra-on-plan-3-2026-09-13.md`), gives the rule the author recommends: the director takes the simplest road — one take when it suffices; the frames of the engine that shot the take (whichever route — the station, a rented card or an external hand; the author's wording made engine-agnostic 2026-09-14 after his correction that the studio has several engines) only when a job needs more than one take or the result breaks; never a pre-split into 4–6; hard cuts, no crossfade in the exam; every endpoint gated before it propagates; two seeds per design. The first plan's "Flux still" was withdrawn — Flux plays no part in a take the local engine (MiniMax H3) shoots (his rulings of 2026-09-04; C68 opened on his words) — **scoped by his word of 2026-09-14 to the local route only:** *"flux kareleri sadece bu bilgisayardaki localdeki model için kapalı. diğer runpod veya api veya mcp için değil. çünkü burada yani localde üretim yaptığımızda herşeyi baştan sonra minimax H3 yapıyor. ok."* — on a rented card, an API or an MCP hand a drawn frame is not closed (the four Flux-drawn presenters stay out of use as recorded 2026-09-13; his word did not reopen them). DONE on that word, and then CORRECTED THE SAME DAY ON HIS ORDER <!-- CEO-OK: continuity-rule-contradictions-removed-2026-09-14 -->: the first pass had only ADDED the rule and left the old doctrine standing beside it (the Creative Director's "six to ten perfect short shots", the Film Director's "six to ten … beat one thirty-second take every time", the still lane's "first and last frames handed to the motion lane", the Editor's "six to ten short generated shots", the product seat's "approved still as the first frame"); he caught it (*"Yeni kuralı yazmışsın ama eski zıt talimatları bırakmışsın … Yalnız yeni cümleyi ekleyip eski emri bırakma"*) and approved the correction (*"Bu düzeltmeyi yapmanı onaylıyorum"*). The sweep covered every seat that applies the road — 12 persona files (10 studio seats + the Prompt / Model Specialist and the Editor held by assignment), 44 sentences replaced; then each seat's prompt was rendered through the runtime loader (`@dxb/voice` `loadPersonaBody`) and the HR compiler (`compilePersonaPrompt`, full and compact) — the FIRST render found 6 of the 12 seats still without the rule in their own words or with an old phrasing left (12/24), so the rule was written into those six in the seat's own terms and two phrasings re-worded; the SECOND render: 24/24 carry the rule and none of the old sentences, an old-phrase sweep of all 16 seat files finds 0; every file re-submitted, gated, bound and verified 12/12 MATCH; tests r31 + b43 + b39 71/71; the seats' status untouched (measured 2026-09-15: all 16 employment_status=active, all 16 legacy status=dormant — the earlier "14 dormant, 2 assigned active" matched no column, audit F021). His four sentences, now the only doctrine on the road: one take when it suffices and no film pre-split into a fixed number of parts · where an engine can shoot several shots in one run that is evaluated first, no separate generations just because there are many shots · when separate takes are needed, continuity is the shooting engine's own frames — the last frame of one take is the first of the next · Flux plays no part when the local engine (MiniMax H3) shoots the take, and no restriction is placed on an external engine's take (RunPod, an API or an MCP hand) — engine words, his correction of 2026-09-14. The measured hold table stays (a limit on take length, not a split). **Then his audit of the same afternoon ("Teslim doğrulandı, fakat çelişki temizliği tamamlanmamış") <!-- CEO-OK: continuity-rule-third-pass-whole-sequences-2026-09-14 -->:** his auditor's live check LIVE_BOUND_MATCH 12/12 held, but three contradictions stood — the storyboard's "the panel is the literal first frame the motion engine receives" beside "never rides into the engine", the Prompt / Model Specialist's "the shot kept short" and "approved frames handed to the engineer for motion", the Film Director's "text-to-video is the wrong one for faces" beside "a written human on the text-to-video road was accepted" — and the check itself was the fault: it looked for one phrase and a list of old words. On his order the WHOLE body (§1–§11) of every one of the 16 seat files was read, sentence by sentence, against his four conditions: 30 more contradicting or stale sentences found and replaced (among them the Film Director's founding "a close-up holds identity for about three seconds … a scene longer than the hold time is several shots, never one" — superseded by the measured one-take 15 s films; the Creative Director's "a six-second shot cut into a thirty-second film beats one thirty-second generation"; the storyboard's "what the engine receives is already the film"; the product seat's "a real photograph in a perfect still"; the Advertising Director's "close-ups planned as separate shots, never asked of one long generation"; the Prompt / Model Specialist's 2026-09-03 "strong default" clause, out of date since his 2026-09-04 22:35 word; the Failure Analysis seat's "the cause is the long single take"), and the road's rule stated in the seat's own terms where a seat lacked it (storyboard, engineer, continuity, screenwriter, editor). The check was rebuilt as a wording check (several wordings per condition plus a contradiction list) — the "20/32 → 32/32" of that hour was a scratch script outside the repo, the kept test had 28 phrase checks and compiled through a path the runtime never calls (found by the evening audit; rebuilt again on the executor's own path — WHERE THIS ROW STANDS, evening); old-phrase sweep 0/16; every changed file re-submitted, gated, bound and verified 16/16; LIVE_BOUND_MATCH 16/16; tests r31 + b43 + b39 71/71; seats' status untouched. The check lives on as `tests/b43/road-consistency.test.ts`. **The same afternoon, his three sentences and his correction of the record's words (amendment (c) above):** the place words "on the station's own road / off the station" — in the 13 seat files that carried them (the other three had none) — replaced by engine words ("for a local-engine take (MiniMax H3 on this card)" / "for an external engine's take"), his canonical sentence written into all 12 applying seats (everything made here on this computer; only the engine that shoots differs; the local engine first, beginning to end; Flux plays no part in a local take; no restriction for an external engine's take; T2V and I2V both open from the start), condition 4 of the test grown to it and the place words made contradictions; delivered, verified 16/16, LIVE_BOUND_MATCH 16/16, the battery green (numbers in the evidence file). **Instruction corrected; not yet tried in production** — the first exam is the first job that needs more than one take; this is not an approval to make a film or start a paid service. Evidence `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/EVIDENCE-continuity-rule-2026-09-14.md`; no code. **(4) THE QC LIST ON THE ROAD — understanding report and plan first, his approval, then code:** its first item was never open — the ruling of 2026-09-03 (the engine never draws lettering) already answers what an engine-drawn mark on a prop is, and the product seat did not apply it to 004's take while 005's verdict did; its second item is a listening hand (the engine's voice against the written lines; three seats wrote "unverified by ear"); wardrobe, flow, object state and a calibrated identity threshold follow. **(5) THE EXTERNAL AUDIT when he brings the auditor** <!-- CEO-OK: external-audit-before-next-leg-2026-09-03 --> — the evidence files above, claim by claim. **(6) THE EXTERNAL HANDS READY — written on his order of 2026-09-14 (*"yapılacak birşey varsa tahtaya yaz sonra vakti geldiğinde yapılsın"*), built when its time comes, after an understanding report, a plan and his approval (Phase 2):** <!-- CEO-OK: external-hands-ready-leg-2026-09-14 --> his doctrine, in his words the same day: the studio has several routes — *"bizde bir kaç yol olacak higgfield onlardan biri, veya minimax h3 API veya başkası. en iyileri en mantıklıları seçilip kullanıma hazır hale entegre edilmeli seçim vakti gelince işe göre duruma göre yapılır"* — and the monthly membership is a running cost of the studio while the holding has advertising work, covering the whole month's production across every job, **never charged to one job or one film** (*"ben bir iş için sadece 59 euro vermeycem"*). READY means three things: each route is one hand in the studio's `media` tool group (`media_submit` with the route as data), its price per finished second in the cost table the CEO reads before the job (his order of 2026-08-31); its key in the vault, never in the repo; and the route passed once with the same brief as the station (the exam) before it is offered. Money out per route (a membership, a prepaid balance) is his approval, one proposal each (B41). **Measured 2026-09-14, the candidates (prices ex-VAT, vendor pages read live; blind-vote Elo from Artificial Analysis, text-to-video with audio / image-to-video; every number and source in `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/EVIDENCE-external-hands-2026-09-14.md`):** ① **Higgsfield Plus over its official MCP** (`mcp.higgsfield.ai`; €47/month billed annually · €59 monthly; 1,200 credits/month, reset monthly (⚠ UNVERIFIED — two third-party sources, the vendor FAQ not read); the "unlimited" models are web-only — every MCP generation deducts credits; Start & End Frame control and image reference on Kling Omni 3): the breadth route — 30+ engines behind one hand; a 15 s ad costs Kling 3.0 1080p 24 credits (≈ 50 ads/month), Kling Omni 3 FLF 18 (≈ 66), Hailuo 2.3 1080p 30 (≈ 40), Wan 3.0 1080p 52.5 (≈ 22), Veo 3.1 1080p 116 (≈ 10), Seedance 2.0 1080p 135 (≈ 8 — the Plus pool is 2.2 minutes of Seedance 1080p a month, so Seedance and Veo there are hero-shot seconds, not volume). Elo: Kling 3.0 1080p 1,108 / 1,077 · Veo 3.1 1,089 / 1,089 · Seedance 2.0 1,220 / 1,197 · Wan 3.0 1,242 / 1,178; Higgsfield's "Hailuo 2.3" is the previous, silent, closed MiniMax generation, not H3. ② **MiniMax H3 on MiniMax's own API** (pay-as-you-go, no membership; 768p $0.08/s · 2K $0.13/s; audio included; the first five reference images free; T2V and Ref2V the same price; not in their prepaid packs yet): the station's own engine family at full size — 15 s = $1.20 / $1.95; Elo 1,226 / 1,190, above Kling and Veo. ③ **fal H3 Max** (MiniMax H3 open weights post-trained by fal on fal's own inference engine, ~35× the official endpoint's throughput; endorsed by MiniMax's H3 team): list price from 2026-09-15 768p $0.08/s · 1080p $0.16/s, Turbo half of that; the 75 %-off launch price ends 2026-09-14; **five generations a day free** for a signed-in account, up to 15 s each — the exam on this route costs nothing; T2V and I2V the same price; audio included; Elo 1,231 / 1,206 (#1 image-to-video with audio). **The author's reading, not a ruling:** for the hero shot the H3 routes (② or ③) are the measured best in price × quality and carry the station's recipes unchanged; Higgsfield is the breadth route for volume and for the engines the station will never hold (Kling, Veo, Seedance); the station stays the free road for everything that needs no more. Not started; nothing integrated; the code of the hands still knows one route (measured 2026-09-14: `media.ts` 311 lines, `media-lanes.ts` 113, `dispatch-book.ts` 430 — RunPod 0, Higgsfield 0, API 0 mentions). <br>**F057 closed · F058 closed · F059 closed · F060 closed · F061 closed · F062 closed · F065 closed — 2026-09-15, W13, on his word *"başla"*, ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE 2026-09-16 (LAW B).** <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b43-road-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w13-studio-contract-registered-2026-09-15 --> The studio was founded on 2026-09-03 and ran twelve days owned by no spec: measured 2026-09-15, word-bounded, DATA_MODEL · EVENT_MODEL · COST_CONTROL · APPROVAL_ENGINE · OBSERVABILITY · WORKFLOW_ENGINE and 00-INDEX carried **0** mentions of it, and the four clock/QA tokens **0** files in the whole corpus outside this board. **Registration only — nothing was built** (guard: no file under `db/` `packages/` `apps/` `tests/` `scripts/` in the commit; migrations 169/169/169; `media_jobs` triggers 0; `approval_rules` 8; `workflows` 0). **F057** DATA_MODEL now carries the job book as it really is — 20 columns, 32 rows