ion ends. Also: decision **U44** in 00-INDEX and requirement rows **MSTU-01…10** in `.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md`, four built and six standing as registered gaps whose owner is W14 on his word. **F028 — waits on his word:** his founding order of 2026-09-03 as a written directive under `docs/ceo-directives/`. A file there carries authority layer 2 in HIS name and a text reconstructed from this row is the author's (the audit's own F003), so none was created; he was asked in the same session and has not answered. Ruler `CHECK-W13-2026-09-15.sh` (md5 `15e3af5ad40340657b4c43fd187c0d92`), dictated by the checker before the first line and committed alone; evidence `EVIDENCE-W13-2026-09-15.md`. **Also open on this row:** Hamza's persona record (v2, file v6 by Opus 5) refused by `enforce_persona_gate_on_activation`'s author list, which never learned U30 — a migration on both engines, parked as B08 step 0 · the project-creation door's missing `name_tr`/`purpose_tr` (set by hand for two projects) · the experts' SDK runs inherit the repository cwd and the session plugins' start context (`cwd` + `settingSources`, one line, behavioural — his call) · the studio's tab itself, gated on B32's approved drawing · the 004 file on disk (4,080,832 bytes) — his word whether it is deleted.<br>**W14 — THE ELEVEN FERRARI LEGS HE ORDERED FIRST, NOW OWNED LEGS ON THIS BOARD. WRITTEN 2026-09-16 ON HIS WORD *"başla"* — AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS BUILT.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> **This is a REGISTRATION, not a construction** — the row's own acceptance test asks for each leg to carry an owner, a CEO-facing deliverable, an acceptance test and a SINGLE proving command, and asks explicitly that nothing be built until he approves. The eight findings the audit left open on this ground — F036, F066, F067, F068, F073, F074, F075, F077 — are each named on the leg that owns it; F073 alone carries four legs, because his engine floor of 2026-08-31 was four orders in one sentence. **THE ONE THING HE SHOULD KNOW BEFORE HE READS THEM:** leg (01) is the two-roads cost table, the paper he needs before choosing between a paid engine and our own card — W14 gives that table an OWNER and a test, it does not hand him the table. When this row closes he holds a promise of it, not the paper. Ruler: `CHECK-W14-2026-09-16.sh` (md5 `37aa18b8ad57f53926a786cb3271b52a`), dictated by the checker session before the first line and committed alone. **THE LEGS:** <!-- W14-L01 --> **(01) THE TWO-ROADS COST TABLE — the paper he must read BEFORE the paid-or-our-own decision** — owner: the AUTHOR session writes it; the CEO is its only reader · finding: F036 · deliverable: one table in Turkish on his studio tab, ONE LINE PER JOB TYPE (a 15-second UGC clip, a 30-second advertisement, a half-hour documentary), and every line carries BOTH roads side by side — what it costs on our own card (electricity at EUR 0.13/h, card hours, operator time) and what the same job costs on a rented or paid engine, with the feasibility verdict beside it · accept: he opens the tab, reads one line, and can say 'paid' or 'our own' without asking a single further question; every number in it traces to a measurement that exists in this repository, and a cell nobody measured reads 'ölçülmedi' instead of a guess · proves: `node scripts/b43/two-roads-table.mjs --check` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L02 --> **(02) THE SHOT ROUTER AS DATA — which shot goes where, in rows he can change, not in code** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the rules live beside the studio's existing routing rows · finding: F073 · deliverable: a router table he can read and change — each kind of shot mapped to the lane that shoots it, stored as database rows rather than buried in a file, with the chosen rule's name written onto the job's own record so he can always see WHY a shot went where it went · accept: a new kind of shot is re-routed by changing ONE row, with no code change and no restart; the job record names the rule that chose its lane · proves: `docker exec -i supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS psql -U postgres -d postgres -At -c "select lane, rule, active from media_routing order by lane"` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L03 --> **(03) THE RUNPOD LANE — the rented machine for when our own card is full or the job is too big** — owner: the AUTHOR session for the lane; the CEO for the rent, because renting is money OUT · finding: F073 · deliverable: a second lane beside our own station: when the card is busy or the job exceeds it, the shot is shot on a rented RunPod machine, and he sees the rent as a figure before it is spent and as a cost row after · accept: one shot runs from start to finish on a rented machine and its euro cost lands in that job's cost rows; the lane stands SWITCHED OFF by default and only his word switches it on, because it spends money outward · proves: `bash scripts/b43/runpod-lane-check.sh` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L04 --> **(04) THE ENGINE x MACHINE MEASUREMENT — what one second of film costs on each engine and each machine** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the bench measurements feed it · finding: F073 · deliverable: a measured grid — every engine down one side, every machine across the top (our own card, each rented size) — each cell saying how long one second of finished film takes there and what that second costs in euro · accept: not one cell is an estimate: each names the run it was measured from, and a cell nobody has measured yet reads 'not measured' rather than a number somebody imagined · proves: `node scripts/b43/engine-machine-matrix.mjs --verify` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L05 --> **(05) THE VISIBLE DIAL — he turns quality up or cost down, and sees the price BEFORE he commits** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the dial's drawing is gated on B32 like every studio screen · finding: F073 · deliverable: a dial on his own screen that he turns with his hand — quality one way, cost the other — with the price of THIS job standing beside it and changing as he turns, so the figure reaches him before the decision instead of after the bill · accept: he moves the dial and the figure beside it changes before anything runs; a job cannot start at all unless that figure was put in front of him first · proves: `pnpm --filter dashboard exec playwright test tests/e2e/studio-dial-cost-before.spec.ts` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L06 --> **(06) THE LONG-FORM HIERARCHY — a job holds scenes, a scene holds shots, so a half-hour film is ONE film** — owner: the AUTHOR session for the records; the Creative Director and Screenwriter seats carry the instruction · finding: F074 · deliverable: the record shape for long films — job, then scene, then shot — so a half-hour documentary stands on his screen as one film with its parts, not as thirty loose clips he has to assemble in his head, and the seats' instructions stop being written for the 15-second one-take world only · accept: a job carrying at least two scenes and four shots exists in the job book and shows on one screen as a single film with its parts; each of the sixteen seats' instructions carries its long-form paragraph · proves: `docker exec -i supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS psql -U postgres -d postgres -At -c "select j.code, count(distinct s.id) as scenes, count(sh.id) as shots from media_jobs j left join media_scenes s on s.job_id=j.id left join media_shots sh on sh.scene_id=s.id group by 1"` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L07 --> **(07) THE DxB AGENCY CHAIN — spawn the sub-company, fill its reel, raise its site, bring it clients** — owner: the CEO owns the first step (spawning a company is an identity act) and the client step; the AUTHOR session owns the rest · finding: F075 · deliverable: the chain he described, in ONE owned place instead of a quotation: the holding spawns a sub-company named DxB Agency, the studio fills its showcase reel from its own films, the reel raises the agency's site, and the site brings the first clients — four steps, each a row with a named owner · accept: each of the four steps is a row with an owner and a gate, and the two steps that create a company or sign a client stop at him; nothing on this chain moves before the machine behind it stands · proves: `node scripts/governance/board-row-exists.mjs dxb-agency-chain` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L08 --> **(08) RIGHTS AND LICENSING — what the holding may legally SELL with each engine, model and music bed** — owner: the CEO decides the licences (a licence is a contract); the AUTHOR session keeps the record · finding: F067 · deliverable: a licence line for every engine, checkpoint and music source the studio touches — saying in one sentence what may be sold with it and what may not — plus the single OpenMontage AGPL question put to him once, in his language, for a yes or a no · accept: no engine, checkpoint or music source may be used on a paying client's job unless its licence line names a commercial right; the AGPL question carries his own answer or is visibly marked as waiting on him · proves: `bash scripts/b43/licence-line-gate.sh` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L09 --> **(09) THE MASTER ARCHIVE AND ITS BACKUP — one disk failure must not erase the films he said yes to** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the nightly backup service carries it · finding: F066 · deliverable: a code-named store holding every master film with its recipe and its seed beside it, inside the nightly backup, and a checksum for each master written into the job book — so a film can be proven whole, and brought back, after the workstation dies · accept: every master film has its checksum in the job book and a copy that is NOT on this workstation; a restore test takes one film out of the backup and brings it back whole and identical · proves: `bash scripts/backup/verify-master-archive.sh` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L10 --> **(10) THE CLIENT LOOP — a brief arrives, a revision round is counted, a delivery profile is read from a table** — owner: Hamza owns the intake door; the AUTHOR session owns the loop and the profiles · finding: F068 · deliverable: the client-facing loop the business has never had: a brief entered through Hamza's chat instead of a script run by hand, a revision round written into the retainer arithmetic so the 8,000-dollar promise matches what the studio actually owes, and one delivery profile per platform (size, frame rate, captions, logo) read from a table rather than guessed at assembly · accept: a brief typed into chat opens a job with no hand-run script anywhere in the path; a revision round is counted against that client's retainer; the assembly step reads its platform profile from the table and never invents one · proves: `node scripts/b43/client-loop-check.mjs` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L11 --> **(11) THE SENIOR-WOMAN PRESENTER BORN IN THE ENGINE — his cast law has no living member for its other half** — owner: the CEO for Safiye's fate; the AUTHOR session for the casting take · finding: F077 · deliverable: a usable elderly-woman presenter for the roster — either his word keeps Safiye, or a text-only casting take in the shooting engine itself gives the holding a senior-woman presenter born where the films are born, needing no retired still to exist · accept: a senior-woman brief can be cast from the roster with no Flux still anywhere in its history; his cast law (men and elderly women) has a living member on BOTH of its halves · proves: `node scripts/b43/cast-roster-check.mjs --senior-woman` · status: planned · gate: his word <!-- /W14 --><br>**W15 — THE LAST ROW OF THE STUDIO PLAN, DONE 2026-09-16 ON HIS WORD *"cetvel gelince başla"*; the checker's TAMAM the same day; **ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE 2026-09-16** (LAW B satisfied).** <!-- CEO-OK: w14-and-w15-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w15-ordered-to-start-on-the-rulers-arrival-2026-09-16 --> **F014 closed · F015 closed · F016 closed · F017 closed · F018 closed · F048 closed · F054 closed · F055 closed · F056 closed.** Four of the nine were already settled by his own registered words of 2026-09-15, so W15 executed their consequences and re-asked him nothing <!-- CEO-OK: law-c-not-a-ceo-law-source-unverified-2026-09-15 --> <!-- CEO-OK: board-rule-like-sentences-are-not-ceo-laws-2026-09-15 --> <!-- CEO-OK: handover-prompt-only-on-his-session-request-2026-09-15 -->. **THE THREE THAT WERE REAL WORK:** **(a) The three handover prompts stopped speaking in his voice.** Each was a paste-ready page written by the author AS HIM; each kept its banner and lost its body (3 first-person lines → 0, in all three). LAW A's reason: a banner saying *"these are not his words"* on top of a page still written in his voice IS the "superseded but retained" form the law names. **THEN HE ORDERED THEM DELETED, AND THEY ARE GONE** <!-- CEO-OK: ceo-delete-the-three-handover-prompt-files-2026-09-16 --> — *"o 3 dosyayı sil"*, 2026-09-16. W15 had removed the false voice and stopped there, because deleting is his call and his standing lesson of 2026-09-05 puts a deletion in front of him first; he was shown the three names, their sizes (1 916 + 1 916 + 2 407 = **6 239 bytes**) and the eight places that named them — all records, no pointer that needed them — and he answered in four words. `git rm`, so every removed line stays addressable in history; the ruler re-run on the deleted tree: F016/F054 PASS, F017 PASS. **(b) The battery is the dxb-verify door's list, WHOLE** — typecheck · `pnpm test` over every file · the ledger gate · i18n · `gitleaks detect` over the whole history · the vitrin gate · the shared W9-B08 battery · a clean tree. Running three folders and calling it the battery is what the door's own sentence forbids. The whole suite on this tree: **129 files, 5–6 red depending on load, every red named in STATE.md with the row that owns it** — B23, B36 ×3, C42 and the new **[[B44]]**. **(c) Personas are bound through a door.** Until 2026-09-16 **no function in the company set `agents.persona_id`**: all **213** bindings were raw UPDATEs from shell scripts — ungated, unaudited, free to drift from `persona_version`. One migration creates `fn_persona_bind` (gate-checked, ownership-checked, writes `persona_version` itself, one audit row per bind and unbind, idempotent, refuses to unbind an ACTIVE employee), applied through the canonical chain to BOTH engines (169 → **170** each). **NOT ONE EXISTING BINDING CHANGED:** `213/219/1e2b5552947189574efcc386b8815358` before and after, company `persona_bind`/`persona_unbind` rows **0**. Every bind path routes through it; raw UPDATE sites **2 files → 0**. Proved on the CONSTRUCTION engine, never the company — one bind row, one unbind row, the active refusal in the door's own words, probe removed whole. **F055 also taught the ledger gate to see a new shape of lie:** a line saying *"done on his word"* asserts his authority exactly as hard as *"CEO-approved"* and passed unseen until today; four such claims stood with nothing behind them, and all four are now registered from his own typed records, one of them correcting a **wrong date** (the GSD commands went on his order of **2026-08-27**, not 2026-08-01 — `git log -S` puts the sentence in e56dcc68). **THE CHECKER'S TAMAM, ROUND 2:** it refused round 1 although every gate was green, for three records defects — the door had only ever been proved to REFUSE and never to OPEN; two ledger keys carried the UTC day instead of the holding's; one banner was still Turkish in an English artefact. All three were measured true, fixed, and re-measured by the checker IN THE FILES. Ruler `CHECK-W15-2026-09-16.sh` (md5 `1cb8ad929eefd1aa1d854a0b59813e61`), dictated before the first line and committed alone. Evidence `EVIDENCE-W15-2026-09-16.md`. **With this row the plan's table W1…W15 is complete on the checker's side. What is left is his eye.**  **F036 closed · F066 closed · F067 closed · F068 closed · F073 closed · F074 closed · F075 closed · F077 closed — 2026-09-16, W14, on his word *"başla"*, **ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE the same day** (LAW B satisfied).** <!-- CEO-OK: w14-and-w15-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w14-eleven-ferrari-legs-registered-on-his-basla-2026-09-16 --> Six of the eight were a gap of OWNERSHIP rather than of machinery — the audit's own words for them are 'has no leg, no owner row', 'is not a leg of the plan', 'has no owner row', 'on no leg' — and what closes such a gap is exactly what W14 wrote: a leg with an owner, a CEO-facing deliverable, an acceptance test and one proving command. F036 had a second half, a records half, and it was closed too: the 2026-09-01 diary still read as though the two-roads cost table had been handed to him. The historical sentence stands word for word — history is not rewritten here — with a dated correction beside it, and the owning spec's section 11 already says in its own second paragraph that it is the ENGINE drawer and NOT the table he asked to read. **THE CHECKER'S TAMAM, 2026-09-16 — AND HIS OWN EYE THE SAME DAY: W14 IS ACCEPTED (LAW B satisfied).** <!-- CEO-OK: w14-and-w15-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 --> The checker session dxb-global-os-c7 (Fable 5.1) withheld its tamam on the first submission (60d95e62) for EIGHT records defects and gave it on the second (519d2fa1) after re-measuring each one in the file rather than in the builder's report: the LAW A residue in STATE 0 · his fourth order carrying its own final period · STATE's 57 commits equal to git's 57 · the $COMPANY_DB fiction 0 on the board against the live docker exec supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS idiom twice · the non-existent test:e2e 0 against the recorded playwright idiom · 'olculmedi' 0 and 'ölçülmedi' 1 · the archive residue 'VIDEO drawer this row owed him' 0 with the clause reading ENGINE drawer and NOT the table he asked to read · and both live exposures written on this board. Its own re-run on the committed tree: ruler w14 PASS 23/23, guard PASS, battery ALL PASS 11/11, ruler md5 intact. **The checker's tamam is not his acceptance** — nothing of W14 has been in front of his eye, and nothing of W14 has been built. **TWO OF THE EIGHT ARE A LIVE EXPOSURE TODAY, NOT ONLY A MISSING OWNER — he must see the risk, not just the row.** F066: the masters of every film he has said yes to sit on ONE disk in this workstation and in no backup — today, this morning, a disk failure erases them, and that stays true until leg (09) is built on his word. F077: the holding has NO usable senior-woman presenter — his own cast law names men and elderly women, and the second half of it has no living member, so the first brief that asks for one cannot be cast, and that stays true until leg (11) is built on his word. The other six were gaps of ownership alone. **WHAT W14 DID NOT DO, said plainly because he is the one it costs:** it built nothing. The two-roads table of leg (01) is not in his hand; he holds an owned promise of it. The eleven legs wait, each on his separate word, and three of them — the RunPod rent, the DxB Agency spawn and the licence contracts — stop at him by the standing approval gate however the work itself is judged. <br>**THE NIGHT CONTENT ENGINE — ORDERED 2026-09-24, PLANNED, NOT BUILT.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> His words: *"onu biizm dxb global os holding projesi için hazıryalabilir miyiz bu özellikte olsun"* — the system shown in vUjAgGa8tAU 00:42–02:30; not a rival-intel source (his correction: *"rakip analizi dedim mi ben sana nerden çıktı"*). While its owner sleeps, it reads the latest short videos of the accounts in a chosen field, transcribes them, scores each one, researches the tools they name, and rebuilds one morning page: hooks, topics, outliers against the account's own 90-day median, and a per-video breakdown. It ends in a weekly script that enters this studio's own hierarchy (script → scenes → shots) on his "evet". Four of the five hands are already in the house at $0: B48's Instagram reading, Speaches, dxb-research, and the resident scheduler. The work is the glue, the tables, the script step and the screen, and the screen stays under B32. **Plan:** `.planning/quick/20260924-night-content-engine/PLAN.md` — *"SIGNAL FOR THE HOLDING"*, rewritten whole the same day from the whole source on his *"herşeyi izle dinle ve sonra planını hazırla"* (the original reel with its sound and 52 frames, the video's system and product sections, and the build prompt kept verbatim beside it in `SOURCE-PROMPT.md`); in his words *"yani bu bir ürün aslında"* — one engine, many desks (the studio, each agency client; OUTLETEURO is not a desk of this product — his word 2026-09-24: *"Outleteuro DxB Holding kurulduktan sonra holding bir lüks marka e-ticaret sitesidir. gerek var şimdlik?"*), nine phases when written, ten since 2026-09-25 (the paid sector review added as Phase 5 on his order, below), the loop closed by reading and analysing every video the studio makes for a client once it is published on the client's account, and our own account's posts once it exists — his word 2026-09-24: *"her müşteriye ürettiğimiz videonun analizini makinamız izlemeli"*; no video is produced only to test. Written by the session dxb-e4, committed by the construction session on his word. Two decisions are his: the paid path if the free hands fall short, and sharing (the engine only reads and proposes); the first desk was answered by his "tamam" of 2026-09-24 22:55 (below; PLAN.md §3a). **THE REVENUE STUDY — ORDERED 2026-09-24, HANDED TO A FABLE 5.1 SESSION ON HIS ORDER, FINISHED THE SAME NIGHT ON HIS WORD:** *"ciddi gelir üretimi şart holdigimiz için"* — worldwide, every continent and language (*"her kıda bulunan en yüksek gelir gelebilecek ülkelere saldırmalıyız"*), research and ideas only, nothing built; brief, the conversations and prior leads in `.planning/quick/20260924-signal-revenue-study/`. Four rounds, three Fable 5.1 sessions, stopped on his *"araştırmayı bitirmeye bak"* (`STUDY.md` the study in Turkish, `EVIDENCE.md`