    45	## Leg of 2026-10-14 — the studio's script seats learn the viewer's mind (content-principles)
    46	
    47	**Ordered 2026-10-14** (his words: *"bu bizim arkadaşın reposu. gerekli yere yaz"*). Source: `github.com/aiwithremy/content-principles` — a friend's repository, one file (`content-principles/SKILL.md`, 10,479 bytes, created 2026-10-13, no licence file), read in full 2026-10-14. It teaches a writer how a short-form viewer's mind works instead of handing it a template: write to one person · the viewer's two questions (is it worth it, how long will it cost) · line 1 must sell line 2 · curiosity loops opened, paid and never deflated · numbers, names and dates instead of summaries · the 10-year-old test on every line · value delivered in the first 3–10 seconds · cut what does not serve the hook · disarm the live objection where it lands · more beats give the edit more cuts. The author's claim of 1.8M views in 30 days rests on his own screenshot — UNVERIFIED.
    48	
    49	Where it goes: the studio's script, hook and copy seats — the SIGNAL night content engine, the Virtual Creator, and client ad scripts. How: through B41's grant chain, as the design seats received `dxb-design` on 2026-10-13 — a studio content skill of our own, written from these principles, with no language limit — the studio writes for clients worldwide, in any language, and leans toward whichever language earns the most in a halal way (his words 2026-10-14: *"nerede para çok kazanıyorsak yani helal yolla o dil üzerine yoğunlaşabiliriz"*) — and with the Islamic boundaries (the "never deflate a loop" principle already forbids the deceptive hook). Before any of its text is copied word for word, the friend's written permission is asked, since the repository carries no licence. Nothing is built before this leg's rank comes in the ordered board.
    50	
    51	**Tested before it is trusted — ordered 2026-10-14** (his words: *"bu repo da bir denensin, test edilsin yani vakti geldiğinde… bir onla onu kullanarak bir yazım, bir onsuz bir yazım yapan iki aynı"*). When this leg's rank comes, before the skill is granted to any seat: two writers, identical in everything — the same model, the same brief, the same description of the viewer — write the same scripts, one with the skill and one without. Several briefs, not one, in more than one language. The pairs are judged blind: the judge, the CEO's eye included, does not know which script came from which writer. Where the studio can publish both versions on its own channels, the real yardstick is what viewers do — how many stay past the first three seconds and how many watch to the end — since that is what the skill itself claims to move. The skill is granted only if the side with it wins.
