   102	## Hyper-realistic UGC — the factory recipe (2026-11-07) <!-- CEO-OK: hyper-realistic-ugc-recipe-2026-11-07 -->
   103	
   104	**His order, 2026-11-07:** UGC and ad videos so realistic — picture, voice, everything — that nobody can tell they are AI. Our own factory is the default (the studio on our own card, free tools; Voice Studio instead of ElevenLabs); paid models are the fallback for the best result. Nothing is built now; it is built at this row's rank in the board's reorder.
   105	
   106	- **The creator's five steps** (reel U1): (1) a real reference — framing, room and light from real TikTok/Pinterest/Reels shots, not a text-to-image picture; (2) a script without "it's not this, it's that" and without short choppy sentences; (3) never the video model's default voice — a cloned voice ("the most important by far"); (4) colour — saturation up, yellows down; (5) frame rate — 24 fps is the giveaway, deliver smoother. His before/after shows two different women, products and rooms, so it proves none of the steps.
   107	- **Testimony** <!-- CEO-OK: ugc-testimony-is-a-real-use-2026-11-07 -->: the AI character may say "I used it" in the first person when the use is real — the product was really used by the CEO, his family, or someone the holding had use it — and that use is recorded with the job. No AI label for now (B28, "The AI label").
   108	- **The factory pipeline, in order:**
   109	  1. Reference: only framing, room, light and phone angle from real UGC go into the LOOK prompt; the face comes from our own cast, never a real person's.
   110	     *Worked example (as told to him):* the client sells a moisturiser. A real skincare clip is found on TikTok or Reels — a woman at her bathroom mirror in morning window light, cream in hand, a towel hanging, the shelf a little messy, the phone held slightly low. That frame goes to the image model as the reference: "same framing, same light, same phone angle and mess; the person is our cast character, the product in her hand is the client's cream." The picture looks phone-shot; the video is moved from it. Taken: the real-life feel (light, angle, room, flaws). Never taken: the person, the face, the content.
   111	     Prompt language: `tools/studio-prompts/realism/ugc-realism-prompts.md` (the 15 modules in phone language, still/klein/H3 forms, this example ready to paste) and its cinema-camera source `realism-prompts.md` beside it (@heyypriyank's sheet, verbatim).
   112	  2. Script: the writer seat; no "not X, Y" or triple short lines, fillers allowed; the WER gate.
   113	  3. Image (his word, 2026-11-07 <!-- CEO-OK: ugc-image-codex-first-seedream-paid-2026-11-07 -->): default = the image tool in Codex on his ChatGPT
   114	     subscription (it routes to a Sunburst-class model), given the real reference — measured best on 2026-11-05: ArcFace against the reference
   115	     Codex 0.89 / H3 Ref2VA 0.86 / FLUX.2-klein 0.80, his eye "mükemmel" (`.planning/quick/20261105-gorsel-karsilastirma/`). Paid beside it:
   116	     Seedream 5 Pro. Local fallback: FLUX.2-klein-4B with a reference (not yet wired into `studio.mjs`).
   117	  4. Video: MiniMax H3 T2VA / Ref2VA, 640×1152, 24 fps.
   118	  5. Voice (his word, 2026-11-07 <!-- CEO-OK: ugc-voice-engine-first-clone-if-better-2026-11-07 -->): the goal is an ultra-natural voice nobody can tell. Default: H3's own voice, born in the take. A clone is used only when it is better — a Voice Studio clone of a consenting cast voice fed to H3 `--ref-audio` (Voice Studio's default engine OmniVoice; VoxCPM2, Apache-2.0, beside it). At this recipe's first setup both are made on the same UGC take and his ear picks the default.
   119	  6. Lip sync, only if `--ref-audio` does not hold: LatentSync 1.5 (8 GB VRAM; 1.6 needs 18 GB and does not fit the 16 GB card).
   120	  7. His eye on the native draft (LAW D).
   121	  8. Grade and grain (FFmpeg): `selectivecolor=yellows='0 0 -0.15 0':correction_method=relative,eq=saturation=1.08,noise=alls=5:allf=t+u` — a starting point that ran clean on the local FFmpeg; the values are his eye's.
   122	  9. Enlarge: SeedVR2 7B-sharp → 1080×1920 (faithful to the face, amendment (j)).
   123	  10. Interpolate, after enlarging: ComfyUI 0.34.0 core `FrameInterpolate` with RIFE 4.25 (Practical-RIFE's own default), ×5 → 120 → `fps=30`; 60 shown beside it for his eye. 120 divides evenly into both; 48 → 30 drops frames unevenly.
   124	  11. Loudness: `loudnorm=I=-14:TP=-1.5:LRA=9` (already in `~/tools/h3/ugc/finish-ugc.sh`).
   125	  12. Final check: WER, identity first ↔ last frame, the picture by eye, the voice by ear.
   126	- **First setup = a trial UGC at once (his word, 2026-11-07):** when this recipe is set up, one full UGC is made end to end on the worked example above — the voice made both ways — and goes to his eye and ear before any client job.
   127	- **What is missing:**
   128	  - Voice Studio is not on disk. Voicebox 0.5.0 is there, stopped, with 0 profiles.
   129	  - No RIFE weight: `models/frame_interpolation` is empty, and the step is not wired into the lane.
   130	  - No take has been shot yet with a cloned voice through `--ref-audio`.
   131	  - The colour recipe is not written into the post script; `post-ugc.sh` keeps a "slightly warm" look on purpose, against step (4).
   132	  - Not measured on this card: SeedVR2 7B-sharp time at 1080, RIFE ×5 time and VRAM.
   133	  - He rejected four local H3 films on 2026-09-01 (`study-cards/minimax-h3.md`); where the factory falls short on a client's shot, the paid fallback is used.
   134	- **Paid fallback** (only where the factory falls short; buying is his):
