    17	**DXB MEDIA STUDIO — the CEO's own room for the advertising business, on the holding's dashboard.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> **⚠ READ THESE ROWS BEFORE TOUCHING THIS ONE — THIS ROW IS THE FACE OF WORK THAT ALREADY EXISTS ELSEWHERE, AND THE CEO ORDERED THE POINTERS PUT HERE SO NO SESSION REBUILDS WHAT IS ALREADY DECIDED:** **[[B28]]** the agency seat itself — the revenue model, the $8,000 retainer, the three scenarios, the engine cost table, the Sora removal and the lifted MiniMax licence · **[[B33]]** the bench — what the card can hold, the capacity ceiling by clip length, the voice-to-cloud lane and the €4/month ceiling on it · **[[B31]]** the armoury, where the tools this studio calls are listed free beside paid · **[[B32]]** the V2 design package — **no screen of this studio may be built before he has approved its drawing** · **[[B10]]** the live board law — *"CANSIZ DÜZ KİTAP GİBİ ORGANİZMA YOK SIFIR CANLILIK"*, which binds this screen like every other V2 screen · **[[B42]]** the arsenal watch, which is what keeps the engine list on this screen from going stale the way LTX-2 and Seedance 2.0 did · **[[B12]]** the voice, because the studio must never be the reason he waits for an answer. <br>**HIS ORDER, 2026-08-31:** *"Holding dashboardunda özel bir DxB Media Studio bölümü olmalı."* <br>**WHAT WILL BE ON HIS SCREEN WHEN THIS ROW CLOSES (law 7, first sentence — no technical word in it):** He opens one tab and sees the advertising business working: which client's job is in hand, the shot list for it, which shots are finished and which are still being made, what each one cost and how long it took, and the finished clips waiting for him to watch and say yes or no — and he says it there, on that screen. <br>**WHICH SINGLE COMMAND PROVES IT:** for the SCREEN not yet nameable — it is fixed in the PLAN that follows B32's approval of the drawing, and the screen may not be drawn before that; the ROAD is planned leg by leg on his approval and is built (BUILT AND STANDING below; corrected 2026-09-15, W2, audit F007). <br>**WHY THE SCREEN IS OPEN AND NOT STARTED (the road IS started — corrected 2026-09-15, W2):** the seat it serves has no client yet (B28), the bench it displays has no gatekeeper yet (B33), and the design package that must draw it has not been approved (B32). **It is written here now so that when those open, the screen is already a row and not a new idea.** <br>**THE LONG-FORM DOCTRINE — HOW THIS STUDIO MAKES A 30-MINUTE FILM, ORDERED BY THE CEO 2026-08-31 AS THE STUDIO'S PRODUCTION LAW.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> **His framing, and it is the whole point of the row:** *"On beş saniyelik ürünler değil yani. Bir de bu uzun videolar nasıl çekilir? Yani mesela yarım saatlik, kırk dakikalık vesaire."* **A half-hour film is never one generation. It is written, broken down, shot by shot, and cut — the way film has always been made — and the studio is built around that hierarchy, not around a prompt box.** <br>**THE HIERARCHY, AND IT IS THE STUDIO'S DATA MODEL, NOT A STYLE NOTE.** A 30-minute piece = **one script** → **8–12 scenes** → **each scene 3–20 second shots** → **every shot generated separately** → **one timeline**. Music, effects, subtitles and transitions land LAST, never inside the generation; the VOICE is the engine's own, born inside the take (tts-cancelled-engine-voice-only-2026-09-04 — the 2026-08-31 "voice-over lands last" superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006)). **Every level of that chain is a record the studio screen must show** — a job has scenes, a scene has shots, a shot has a state, a cost and a clock. The shot is the atom of this business; B33's card time and B28's retainer are both denominated in it. <br>**⚡ THE RULE THAT DECIDES THE ECONOMICS — AND IT IS THE MOST VALUABLE LINE ON THIS ROW.** **A 30-minute video does not mean 30 minutes of generated video.** Cut properly, **only 20–40% of a professional half-hour is true video-generation**; the rest is narrated stills with zoom and pan, motion graphics, type, product photography, screen capture and B-roll (how a narrated passage is VOICED after the TTS cancellation of 2026-09-04 is not yet ruled — an open question for him, audit F010; the engine's own voice is the only voice on record). **Costed 2026-08-30 from ONE take on this machine — HISTORY, not a price:** (B42 — a 15.08 s delivery shot at 1152×640 costs 10 min 20 s, a 5 s draft at 864×480 costs 90 s; the 5 s delivery figure of ~3.4 min is DERIVED, ⚠ not yet measured; the later measurements of amendment (i) — +37 % card per finished second on an 8-shot film, post 37 % of a film's clock — are NOT folded into the table below, so a recomputation is owed before any price rests on it; audit F070, labelled 2026-09-15): <br>**THE COST OF ONE 30-MINUTE FILM, BY HOW MUCH OF IT IS ACTUALLY GENERATED — generated seconds · shots at ~6 s · card hours including finals and 3:1 drafts:** **EVERYTHING GENERATED, the wrong way** → 1,800 s · ~300 shots · **~34 h** ⟶ **40% GENERATED** → 720 s · ~120 shots · **~16 h** ⟶ **20% GENERATED** → 360 s · ~60 shots · **~8 h**.<br>**A half-hour documentary edited the professional way costs about ONE NIGHT of one card. Edited the naive way it costs a working week.** The edit is not a finishing step in this business — **it is the single biggest cost lever the studio has**, and the screen must show the generated-percentage of every job because that number is the margin. <br>**CONTINUITY IS AN ASSET THE STUDIO HOLDS, NOT A HOPE IT CARRIES.** *"Adam bir sahnede siyah ceket giyiyorsa sonraki shot'ta birden mavi ceket olmamalı. Araba aynı kalmalı. Mekân değişmemeli. Işık yönü tutarlı olmalı."* **A job that needs continuity across takes holds a REFERENCE SET** — character, wardrobe, location, product, palette, lens and camera language — **and on this station that set is the frames of the engine's own take, never a drawn still handed in** (astra-rule-accepted-flux-scoped-to-local-2026-09-14; flux-local-engine-only-everything-made-here-2026-09-14): one take when it suffices; when a job needs more than one, the last frame of one take is the first of the next, on whichever route; an external engine's take may also be handed a still made here. The 2026-08-31 "every job opens with a MASTER REFERENCE SET before one shot is generated … a shot generated without the reference set is scrap" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006) — the four films he accepted are one prompt, one take, no reference set (road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04). <br>**THE THREE ENGINE TIERS — AND THE STANDING BAN ON DEPENDING ON ONE SUPPLIER.** *"Ben tek bir Gemini aboneliğine bel bağlamazdım."* The studio routes every shot to one of three tiers and the router is part of the build: **① DIRECTOR** — script, shot list, continuity, QA: the creative brain, Claude Fable 5.1 at effort xhigh, Opus 5 the disabled standby (studio-brain-fable-5-1-opus-5-standby-2026-09-05; the 2026-08-31 "Claude Opus 5 / GPT / Gemini" was his example, superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006)) — a DEFAULT, not a restriction: the director and the screenwriter always the smartest model of the day, other seats Opus 5 by default, any brain switchable by him or Hamza with one click, new models addable inside the studio — his word of 2026-09-15, amendment (l) below. **② PREMIUM HERO** — the few shots the client's eye lands on: the strongest closed models of the day (Veo-class), bought per shot. **③ VOLUME ENGINE** — the many shots nobody pauses on: MiniMax H3 (the only one measured on this station), Wan 2.2 and LTX-2.5 as study cards, local or rented. **Reference images, where a route takes them:** for a take the LOCAL engine shoots, NO drawn still is handed to the engine — the take is made from text and every generated face is born in the engine (flux-local-engine-only-everything-made-here-2026-09-14; ahmet-cast-member-born-in-engine-2026-09-04); for an EXTERNAL engine's take a still made here — FLUX.1-Krea on this card or a subscription hand (Antigravity CLI at $0.00 per image, ChatGPT Image 2) — may be handed, without restriction beyond the brief's road (the 2026-08-31 "reference images come from … Flux/OpenAI-class" as a general rule is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006)). **The VOICE is the engine's own, measured by WER against the script — "Voice from TTS" is CANCELLED** (tts-cancelled-engine-voice-only-2026-09-04, superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006)); **assembly from FFmpeg/Remotion/DaVinci — no card needed for that.** **No tier may become the only path: if one supplier closes, raises its price or sunsets its API — as Sora 2 will on 2026-09-24 (OpenAI's notice of 2026-03-24, B42; not yet measured — corrected 2026-09-15, W2, audit F086) — the studio changes one route and keeps producing.** That is the lesson B42 exists to enforce. <br>**THE SHAPE OF ONE ORDER, END TO END.** The CEO's own example: *"OutletEuro için 20 dakikalık video hazırla"* → script → storyboard → ~150 shots → generation routed across the three tiers → voice-over → subtitles → music → render → **his accept or reject on this screen**. **The studio is the thing that turns one sentence into that chain and shows him every link of it while it runs.** <br>**AND THE WORKFORCE IS ASSIGNED TO IT, NOT BORROWED FOR IT — HIS ORDER: *"holdingimizde 220 kişilik uzman var departmanlar var bu studio bölümünde görevlendirilmeliler."*** The studio is not a tool one employee opens; it is a department with named seats — director, scriptwriter, storyboard, reference-set keeper, shot producer, continuity QA, voice, editor, delivery. **✓ THE HEADCOUNT IS SETTLED BY THE CEO, 2026-08-31: *"205 doğru olan."*** <!-- STATE: b43-headcount-2026-08-31 = 205 @ 2026-08-31 --> <!-- CEO-OK: headcount-205-settled-2026-08-31 --> Four numbers were in circulation — he had said 220, the persona files counted 200 across 23 departments, the live company database reported **205 agents**, and B28's middle scenario assumed 63. **He ruled for the database's own figure, which is the one that can be re-measured on every battery run rather than trusted from a document.** The 63 in B28's Orta scenario is therefore an ASSUMPTION about how many clients one workforce serves, **not a headcount**, and B28 must be read that way. <br>**═══ THE ENGINE FLOOR OF THIS STUDIO — AND IT IS AN EXAMPLE, NOT A SPECIFICATION ═══** <br>**⚡ THIS SECTION IS DELIBERATELY OPEN, BY CEO ORDER 2026-08-31 — READ THIS BEFORE YOU READ ANYTHING BELOW IT.** *"Bu bölüm tamamiyle geliştirilmeye; Ferrari seviyesine ve uluslararası yarışmalarda birinciliğe aday seviyeye çıkarılmaya açık bir bölümdür. Burayı okuyan Opus 5 eğer çok daha iyi bir upgrade planı kafasında zihninde varsa bu bahsettiğimiz seviyelere çıkaracak mimariyi oluşturabilir zira bu bizim için sadece bir örnekti. Bu bölümü kendisi araştırıp test edip belki de daha iyisini kurup onu da test edip hangisi iyi ise onu seçmesi gereklidir zira bu bölüm HOLDING'İN ÇOK ÖZEL BÖLÜMLERİNDENDİR."* **Everything below is one worked example. A session that can prove a better architecture must BUILD it, TEST both, and keep the winner on evidence — not adopt this one because it is written down.** <br>**AND THE STANDING DUTY THAT COMES WITH IT — LAZINESS IS FORBIDDEN ON THIS ROW.** *"Her motor modelin istasyonumuzda yerel olarak çalıştırabilecek versiyonu da araştırılmalıdır bu konuda tembellik asla yapılmamalıdır. Ör: biz minimax h3'ü yerele kurduk. Kurulamayanlar runpod sisteminde kurulabilir."* **For every engine the question is asked in this order and the answer is MEASURED, never read off a requirements table: (1) can it run on OUR station — quantised, offloaded, however it takes? (2) if not, RunPod. (3) if not, the external hands — a membership over MCP or a pay-as-you-go engine API (his correction of 2026-09-14: "API" had been the wrong word).** **H3 is the precedent and the standard:** a 33B model produces 15-second audio-video here on a 16 GB card because someone did the work. A session that reports "it needs 4 GPUs" without trying has not done its job. <br>**THE QUALITY LAW — THE WORK MUST NOT LOOK LIKE AI VIDEO.** The bar is *"Nike, Apple, Mercedes, Coca-Cola reklamı gibi gerçek çekilmiş sinematik reklam hissi"* — a shot that reads as FILMED. **That bar is never reached by picking a better model.** It needs five things at once: **the model · the references (on this station the engine's own frames) · camera control · enlargement only after his eye accepts the native draft, on his word (LAW D, law-d-draft-first-upscale-last-2026-09-03) · post-production.** Owning only the first and promising the bar is a lie to the client. <br>**WHAT IS HOSTABLE AND WHAT IS NOT — READ FROM VENDORS AND LEADERBOARDS, 2026-08-31; NOTHING HERE IS MEASURED ON THIS STATION EXCEPT H3** (heading corrected 2026-09-15, W3, audit F092)**.** **Closed, API only:** Veo 3.1 · Seedance 2.5 · **Wan 3.0** (shipped 2026-08-06 as API-only beta; **no weights on HuggingFace, GitHub or ModelScope** — Alibaba's last open flagship is still Wan 2.2, Apache 2.0) · Kling 3.0 · Runway Gen-4.5. **Open weights, ours to host:** **MiniMax H3** · **LTX-2.5** · Wan 2.2 · HunyuanVideo 1.5 — and **the open shelf can be fronted by ONE launcher, WanGP (Wan 2.1/2.2, LTX, HunyuanVideo, Qwen Image, Flux), with H3 beside it as the engine WanGP does not carry — but WanGP is a STUDY CARD, NOT installed on this station** (measured 2026-09-14 and 2026-09-15: no WanGP directory under /home/dxb; 0 Wan/LTX/Hunyuan weight files; the card holds MiniMax H3 — FL2VA Q4_K, Ref2VA fp8 — and FLUX.1-Krea-dev fp8 only; `study-cards/wan2gp.md` Status: STUDY; audit F005). <br>**WHY H3 IS THE FIRST CHOICE, ON NUMBERS.** Artificial Analysis open-weights text-to-video with audio, measured 2026-08-31: **MiniMax H3 Elo 1,227 · LTX-2.5 Pro 1,061 · LTX-2.5 Fast 1,060** — H3 leads the open field by **166 Elo** and sits in the closed leaders' league on the general audio-video board. **Its two checkpoints, as engine facts: FL2VA** does text→video, first-frame→video and **first-frame + last-frame→video**; **Ref2VA** takes **up to 9 images, 3 videos and 3 audio references in one generation**. **Which road a take runs on comes from the BRIEF — text-to-video the default, image-to-video open, "choose the best" allowed** (road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04; t2v-i2v-expert-choice-2026-09-03); on this station a take is shot from text with no drawn frame handed in, and a reference is a frame of the engine's own earlier take (2026-09-14). The 2026-08-31 "the perfect frame is built first and the model is only asked for motion … Ref2VA, not text-to-video, is the capability this business sells" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006) — every film he has accepted was made on the text road. <br>**THE WRONG WAY AND THE WAY THIS STUDIO WORKS.** Wrong: `"Mercedes driving through Dubai at night, cinematic"` → generate → hope. **Right, as the road stands after his September rulings:** ① the BRIEF decides the road — text-to-video by default, pictures when the brief brings them (road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04) · ② the prompt written as a cinematographer writes it (*50mm anamorphic, low-angle tracking, subtle handheld vibration, realistic suspension physics, reflections moving across bodywork, wet asphalt, volumetric street lighting*) — product, logo, light, camera all in the words, the engine never drawing lettering (no-brand-restriction-2026-09-03) · ③ ONE take when it suffices — the accepted films are one prompt, one take, ≤ 15 s · ④ when a job needs more than one take, continuity is the shooting engine's own frames, the last of one take the first of the next; close-ups (headlight, wheel, badge, interior) are further takes only when the job needs them · ⑤ **never a pre-split into a fixed number of parts** (astra-rule-accepted-flux-scoped-to-local-2026-09-14). The 2026-08-31 "a flawless hero frame first … 6–10 perfect shots of 3–5 seconds, cut into 30 seconds" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006); nobody asks one model to get 30 seconds right, and nobody cuts a film into pieces by count. <br>**THE ROUTER — WHICH SHOT GOES WHERE (data, not code, so an engine can be swapped without touching the studio) — NOT BUILT, no leg carries it yet (audit F073; a planning item, W14).** His example routing, read through the brief's-road rule: product/hero → **H3** on the road the brief names (text by default) · people, lifestyle, client references → **H3 Ref2VA** where a route takes references · a cut sequence in one run → **LTX-2.5** (native multi-shot — a study card, unmeasured here) · cheap variations at volume → **Wan 2.2** (a study card, unmeasured here). **What happens to the shot after the engine returns it is the production line below, not the router's business.** <br>**═══ THE PRODUCTION LINE — THE ORDER OF OPERATIONS FOR ONE FINISHED SHOT, AND IT BEGINS WITH THE BRIEF'S ROAD. CEO ORDER 2026-08-31, READ THROUGH HIS SEPTEMBER RULINGS** (the 2026-08-31 heading "it begins with an image, not a prompt" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006): road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04)**.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> **His own worked example, and it is a division of labour before it is a pipeline:** *"Senaryo Claude Opus 5, resimler ChatGPT Image 2 ile üretilir, video MiniMax H3 gibi kiralayacağımız veya yereldeki modellerle üretilir. Bu bir örnek."* **THE CHAIN, IN ORDER — no step may be skipped and none may be folded into the one before it (each step as the September rulings left it; the 2026-08-31 wording of steps 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9 is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006)):** **(1) SCRIPT & DIRECTION** — the creative brain (Claude Fable 5.1 at xhigh, Opus 5 standby) writes the script, the shot list and the continuity rules · **(2) THE REFERENCE SET — where the job needs continuity across takes**; on this station it is the frames of the engine's own take, never a drawn still built before the first generation · **(3) THE IMAGE — stills, panels, first frames, all made HERE on this computer** (the image lanes below) **and handed only to an EXTERNAL engine's take; Flux plays no part in a take the local engine shoots** · **(4) MOTION — the road comes from the brief: text-to-video the default, image-to-video open; the engine standard 4 sampling steps at the native draft** (engine-standard-4-steps-no-upscale-unless-asked-2026-09-04) · **(5) THE NATIVE DRAFT MASTER** — 640×1152 vertical / 864×480 horizontal, the engine's own output, judged by HIS EYE first (LAW D) · **(6) ENLARGEMENT — only after his eye accepts the draft and on his word; 1080 the ceiling for UGC, 2K enough, no 4K; SeedVR2 the measured enlarger** (law-d-draft-first-upscale-last-2026-09-03; amendment (j)) · **(7) COLOUR GRADE + FILM GRAIN** · **(8) AUDIO — the engine's own voice born in the take (no TTS, no recorded or cloned voice); music and mix in post** · **(9) ASSEMBLY — one take when it suffices; several takes only when the job needs them, continuity by the shooting engine's frames, never a fixed count** (FFmpeg / Remotion / DaVinci). **Steps 6 through 9 DO use the card here** — RealESRGAN ×4 ran 2.09 s per frame, 37 % of a film's clock (measured 2026-09-01, amendment (i)); the 2026-08-31 "need no card at all" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006) — the card is still never the whole cost of a job. <br>**WHY STEP 3 STAYS ITS OWN STEP — FOR THE ROUTES THAT TAKE A FRAME (an external engine's take); on this station no frame is handed to the engine at all.** A still can be regenerated fifty times for less than one second of video, judged by eye and corrected — product wrong, logo wrong, wheel wrong, light wrong, face wrong. **A video engine cannot repair a frame it was handed; it can only move it.** So where a route takes a frame, the studio spends its judgement at the CHEAPEST point in the chain and asks the expensive engine for motion only. The 2026-08-31 "a shot generated from a prompt instead of from an approved frame is scrap by policy" is superseded in place 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006): on the brief's text road the take IS made from the prompt (road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04), and on this station no still is handed to the engine (flux-local-engine-only-everything-made-here-2026-09-14) — the image lane stays an engine of this studio for the external routes and for everything that is not a take. <br>**⛔ DO NOT START WITH LTX-2.5's NVFP4 CHECKPOINT, THOUGH IT LOOKS LIKE THE OBVIOUS BLACKWELL PICK.** `ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-transformer-nvfp4.safetensors` (18.7 GB) is the smallest file in the repo and **three separate reporters have it failing in ComfyUI** — one on an RTX 5090 running **exactly this holding's stack** (Ubuntu · ComfyUI 0.32 · PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130), dying at the first sampling step with `RuntimeError: mat1 and mat2 shapes cannot be multiplied (3520x4096 and 2048x4096)`. Lightricks has acknowledged it. The working path today is **INT8-ConvRot at 22.666 GiB resident**, which does not fit this station — **so LTX-2.5 is a rented-bench engine UNTIL a smaller quantisation exists, and the standing duty above applies: look for it every time, do not assume.** <br>**THE IMAGE HAND IS PART OF THE ENGINE FLOOR, NOT AN ACCESSORY — CEO ORDER 2026-08-31: *"sadece subscriptionlar değil yerelde de imageler üretilebilir en kaliteli seviyede ama olmalı. çünkü video motorları onlarla ürün çıkaracak."*** On the external routes every hero frame, product reference and character sheet is an IMAGE made here, and those engines are only as good as what they are given; on this station the take is made from text and the cast is born in the engine (2026-09-04 / 2026-09-14). **Three lanes, all live:** the free subscription hands already connected (**Antigravity CLI** via Google AI Pro at $0.00/image, and **ChatGPT Image 2** through the holding's existing **Plus** membership, which must be wired directly into this studio) · **and a LOCAL image stack at the highest quality the station can reach** — FLUX.1-Krea-dev fp8 in ComfyUI on this card (installed and measured: it drew the 2026-09-01/02 presenters); Qwen Image and z-image are study cards; WanGP is NOT installed (audit F005, corrected 2026-09-15, W3). **The local lane is not the cheap fallback; it is what makes the studio independent, and it must be brought to the same quality bar as the paid hands.** <br>**NO SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE, AND THE MACHINE UNDERNEATH IS A DIAL — CEO ORDER 2026-08-31.** *"Sistem öyle mükemmel kurulmalı ki, runpod olmazsa API ile en makul modellere bağlanıp yapılmalı."* **Three lanes in order: ① our own station · ② RunPod, the machine chosen per engine and per job · ③ the external hands — a monthly membership reached by MCP (Higgsfield) or a pay-as-you-go engine API (MiniMax H3 official, fal H3 Max), several of them integrated and READY, the one for a job chosen when the job comes (his correction of 2026-09-14: "API" had been the wrong word for the membership route; leg (6) below).** **And "most reasonable" does NOT mean cheapest — he defined it:** *"en makulden kastım örneğin higgsfield'da API ile MCP ile bağlanıldı ama seedance 2.5'da veya wan 3.0 da daha uygun ve daha mükemmel sonuç tam sinematik çekim olacaksa orası seçilebilir. Kârlı durumlarda holding çalışanlarımız kaliteyi hedef edinmelidir."* **When the job is profitable, the target is QUALITY, and the closed leaders (Seedance 2.5, Wan 3.0, Veo) are legitimate choices — this is D1-bis (B41) applied to video, not an exception to it.** <br>**THE DIAL MUST BE VISIBLE AND TURNABLE — BY THE AGENTS AND BY THE CEO HIMSELF.** His scenario is this part's acceptance test: *"bir müşteri geldi çok yoğun bir reklam işi istiyor ve aynı zamanda kanallarımız için de belgesel ve islami içerikler üretimi de olacak — bunların hepsinin aynı zamanda olması için eğer daha yüksek makina kiralanması gerekiyorsa efektif şekilde ajanlarımız tarafından yapılabilmeli."* When three jobs land at once an agent sizes the rented machine up, runs them in parallel, and sizes back down when they finish — **and the cost is computed and SHOWN before the decision, never discovered on an invoice.** *"çalışanlarımızın eli kolu ayağı, kullanacakları aletler vs herşey kolayca erişilebilir, substitute edilebilir olmalı; maliyet tablosu da hesaplanmalı."* **⚠ AND IT IS NOT A HIDDEN DIAL — HIS EXPLICIT CORRECTION: *"changeable derken bende görebilmeliyim yani kapalı changeable değil; changeable bölümünü istersem ben de değiştirebilirim."* Every engine route, every machine choice and every price sits on THIS screen where he can read it and override it himself.** **⛔ The money boundary of B41 is untouched: the agent may size, propose and price — renting a bigger machine is money out, so it surfaces to him as ONE proposal carrying its cost. The bench proposes, it never buys.** <br>**THE ENGINE × MACHINE TABLE IS A MEASUREMENT AND IT IS STILL OPEN.** H3 runs quantised on 16 GB; LTX-2.5's working checkpoint needs 32 GB today. **Renting every engine on the same card would eliminate LTX unfairly**, so B28's five-engine exam must price **engine × machine** and report quality, seconds per shot, and cost per delivered shot — 5090 32 GB · A6000/A40 48 GB · A100 80 GB · H100 80 GB. **$0.99 is not automatically the answer.** <br>**═══ TWO ROADS, PRICED SIDE BY SIDE — WHAT IS DOABLE WITH MONEY AND AT WHAT COST, WHAT IS DOABLE WITHOUT MONEY AND AT WHAT COST. CEO ORDER 2026-08-31, AND HE TOLD US IT ALREADY EXISTS ON THIS BOARD.** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> *"Bu bölümde aynı zamanda şu da olmalı: paralılarla yapılabilirlik ve cost, parasızlarla yapılabilirlik ve cost — bununla ilgili tahtada birşeyler yazıldı, lütfen onu bul, önce hazırlamam lazım."* **THE THING HE REMEMBERED IS FOUND: [[B31]] section 8 of `CAPABILITY_ARSENAL_DOCTRINE.md`, the PAID PROPOSAL BENCH — six rows already priced, each already naming its free alternative** (Apify from $19/mo, apify.com/pricing read 2026-09-24, vs scrapling+camoufox · Composio $99/mo · HeyGen ~$24-72/mo · Seedance per-credit · Gemini omni-video per-minute, measured: **Veo 3.1 $0.40 / $0.12 / $0.08 per second, Nano Banana 2 Lite $0.0336 per image, API free tier zero** · paid LiteLLM models), **plus `socialforge` and kie.ai added on his own order.** **BUT A POINTER IS NOT THE DELIVERABLE HE ASKED FOR.** This row owes the VIDEO DRAWER of that bench, **as a table on this screen**, one line per job type — hero product shot · people and lifestyle · multi-shot sequence · bulk variations · image and reference · voice · assembly — **carrying BOTH roads in the same row: the free way with its feasibility and its true cost (card hours, electricity, operator time), and the paid way with its feasibility and its price.** *"Önce hazırlamam lazım"* — **he intends to READ this table and decide from it, so it is a CEO-facing artefact, not an engineering note** — NOT delivered: `CAPABILITY_ARSENAL_DOCTRINE.md` §11 is the engine drawer (per engine, in English), not this table, and no open leg carries the table yet (audit F036; a planning item, W14 — nothing built before his word)**.** <br>**AND THE FREE ROAD IS NOT EMPTY — HIS OWN CORRECTION, WHICH FORBIDS RE-RESEARCHING WHAT WE ALREADY OWN: *"Open source olanlar zaten bizim WanGP'deki 6 motorları var."*** Those six (Wan 2.1/2.2 · LTX · HunyuanVideo · Qwen Image · Flux behind the WanGP launcher, plus H3 beside it) are **open-weight candidates at zero licence cost — and, except MiniMax H3 and FLUX.1-Krea, they are STUDY CARDS, NOT INSTALLED on this station** (measured 2026-09-14 and 2026-09-15: no WanGP directory, 0 Wan/LTX/Hunyuan weight files, `study-cards/wan2gp.md` Status: STUDY). **His sentence of 2026-08-31 had been written onto this row as a measured fact — "HELD, installed" — without a measurement; corrected 2026-09-15 (W3, audit F005, RULE #0-A).** A session may not research the six as unknowns, and may not schedule one as held: each is installed and MEASURED on this card before it is offered (bench law 3, B33). **The paid road exists to be BEATEN by that shelf wherever the shelf can do the job, and to be bought — through B41's money boundary, as one priced proposal — only where it cannot.** <br>**AND THE STUDIO IS NOT THE END OF THIS — DXB AGENCY IS, CEO ORDER 2026-08-31.** *"holding DxB Agency adında bir sub şirket spawn etmeli ve burada müşteri çekebilmek için örnek mükemmel reklam videoları oluşturulmalıdır. Sonra bu sitenin pazarlaması yapılmalıdır. Tüm herşey end to end holding yapmalı; uluslararası pazardan müşteriyi bağlayacak herşeyi tasarlamalı ve başarmalıdır."* **The chain he ordered, end to end: spawn the subsidiary → produce a showcase reel good enough to win a brand → build and market its site → win international clients → deliver through this studio.** **The showcase is not a demo — it is the first product, and the quality law above applies to it before it applies to any client.** This binds to B28, which holds the seat, the retainer and the roster; **B43 is where the work is done and shown, B28 is where the money is counted.** <br>**WHAT "SUBSIDIARY" MEANS HERE — HE DEFINED IT HIMSELF, 2026-08-31, AND IT IS NOT A LEGAL ENTITY.** *"Şirketten kastım sanal şirket: holding içinde adı ve çalışanları olan, dashboard üzerinden içine girip bakabildiğimiz, kendi websitesi olan."* **DxB Agency is a VIRTUAL company inside the holding** — it has a name, it has staff, the CEO opens it from the dashboard and looks inside it, and it has a website of its own facing the outside world. **It is a room in this OS, not a registration at a registry.** <br>**AND ITS STAFF ARE THE HOLDING'S OWN — HIS CORRECTION THE SAME DAY, WHICH CLOSES A MISREADING BEFORE IT COULD BE BUILT.** *"Çalışanları olan derken holdingimizin sorumlu departmanları ve çalışanları kastettim. Ekstra çalışana, ayrıca uzman personaya, spesifik işi yapacak kişilere ihtiyaç varsa İK tarafından kadroya alınmalı."* **No parallel workforce is invented for this agency.** The responsible departments and the employees already on the holding's roster — **205 settled by him 2026-08-31; the roster measured since: 219 on 2026-09-03, active 213** (audit F091) — are ASSIGNED to it; the agency is a room they work in, not a second payroll. **And where a seat genuinely does not exist — a specific craft the roster cannot cover — it is HR that opens it**, through the holding's own persona pipeline (`personas/`, the `dxb-persona` door), as a hire into the same roster. **A studio seat that is not a named employee of this holding is a defect, not a shortcut.** <br>**THE WEBSITE IS A SALES INSTRUMENT, AND ITS CONTENT IS THE PRODUCT ITSELF.** *"İşte bu webte 3D, animasyon vb reklamların üretimi olmalı; çok ama çok kaliteli reklam örnekleri web içinde olmalı ki müşteri görünce hemen bize reklam versin. Ve bu müşterilerin baştan sona reklam kampanyaları da holding tarafından yapılsın."* The site carries **3D, animation and film work at a level that closes a client on sight** — and what it sells is not clips but **whole campaigns run end to end by the holding.** <br>**⛔ AND THE ORDER OF BUILD IS HIS, EXPLICITLY, SO NO SESSION STARTS AT THE WRONG END: *"lakin önce sistem, sonra web ve kampanya falan."*** **① The system that produces (this row's engine floor and the studio screen) → ② the site that shows it → ③ the campaigns it sells.** A session that builds the website before the studio can produce the work to fill it has inverted his order. <br>**⚠ NOTHING IN THIS SECTION IS MEASURED ON THIS STATION EXCEPT H3.** The Elo figures, the VRAM figures and the hostability column are read from vendors and leaderboards. **Bench law 3 (B33) governs: a tool not measured on this card may not be scheduled, and no clip length, quality or price may be promised to a client on a number that came from a website.** <br>**═══ WHERE THIS ROW STANDS — 2026-09-15 morning. The audit handoff of 2026-09-14 (`STUDIO_AUDIT_HANDOFF.md`, immutable, 111 findings) is being worked on the implementation branch `studio/b43-ferrari-implementation-20260915` (cut from the snapshot `a6fdfdde`; master untouched): W1 his two words registered (accepted by him) · W2 the records brought to the truth · W2b his three rulings ("LAW C" no law; board rule-like sentences no laws; handover prompt only on request) · W3 this row's doctrine under LAW A in place · W4 the owning specs, and his brain ruling (defaults Fable 5.1 / Opus 5, any brain switchable by him or Hamza, new models addable — B08 step 7) · W4b his auditor's three findings corrected, his cast addition registered (a client may order female-presenter content, on the client's responsibility). Every W after W1 waited for his eye, and on 2026-09-16 he gave it in one sentence over the whole road <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b43-road-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 -->. **W5 AND W9 ARE FINISHED AND ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE — they wait on nothing** (corrected 2026-09-19, LAW A: the sentence here still said he had closed the session without answering either, which stopped being true at 2026-09-15 15:5x; he caught it himself): W5 (the 16 seats — cast law + his addition, three roads, no voice residue, 4 steps, no model name) under `studio-seats-w5-to-w6c-accepted-2026-09-15` <!-- CEO-OK: studio-seats-w5-to-w6c-accepted-2026-09-15 -->, and the W9 plan for the two assigned seats (EVIDENCE-W4b) under `w9-assigned-seats-plan-approved-2026-09-15` then `studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-15` <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-15 -->. The not-yet-built studio legs keep waiting for their turn, leg by leg, on his word. Evidence per W: `EVIDENCE-W1…W4b-2026-09-15.md`. ═══ WHERE THIS ROW STANDS — 2026-09-14 evening. On his order (*"en son yapılanları önce bir denetle … hatalar varsa düzelt … tek tek sırayla"*) the day's work was audited — three read-only Fable 5.1 auditors and the author's re-reading — and every fault fixed in order: the Sound seat's replacement voice (against his voice ruling of 2026-09-04; the seat had never been read against it), enlargement before his eye (against LAW D; step 7 → step 10), the real-photograph-only gate (against the written-human road and the engine-born cast), the still-first / short-shot / strong-road residue in ten seats, the road check (rebuilt on the executor's own prompt path, 16 seats, proved on a mutated copy 8/8), the approval gate (every CEO-OK marker on a line checked, 118 → 193; a stale id of 2026-09-04 found in the archive and corrected), and these records. All 16 seats gated and bound at their latest versions (63 `persona.bound` rows today); nothing tried in production. <!-- CEO-OK: audit-of-the-days-work-corrected-2026-09-14 --> Evidence `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/EVIDENCE-audit-2026-09-14.md`; STATE 2026-09-14 evening block. ═══ WHERE THIS ROW STANDS — 2026-09-14 daytime. The diary of how the studio was built and tested, 2026-09-01 → 2026-09-13 (the engine-floor test he rejected, the founding, the night of the two drafts, the hands, plan ①, plan ②, the clock), was moved WHOLE from this row to `.planning/STATE-ARCHIVE.md` § "B43 — the diary" on his order of 2026-09-14, nothing deleted; the rulings behind it are the 35 entries dated 2026-09-03 → 2026-09-13 in `scripts/governance/ceo-approvals.json`; the evidence, claim by claim, is in `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/`. ═══** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> <br>**═══ WHERE THIS ROW STANDS — 2026-09-19 evening. HE CAUGHT THE RECORD DENYING AN ACCEPTANCE HE HAD GIVEN, AND THE CLASS GOT ITS RULER. Opening the day he was told two studio items still needed his word; his eye had covered both on 2026-09-15 <!-- CEO-OK: studio-seats-w5-to-w6c-accepted-2026-09-15 --> <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-15 -->. He named the Fable 5.1 session chief engineer and the Opus 5 session its builder, and ordered the plan with its ruler, applied letter by letter <!-- CEO-OK: records-ruler-ordered-on-his-word-2026-09-19 -->. **Seven commits, none of them accepted (LAW B):** `a26bdd2d` the records ruler (`tests/b43/records-truth.ts`, four rules) · `9e43399f` six sentences of the records corrected, each naming the ledger entry behind it, and his order registered · `3beb0295` the knowledge graph 218 commits behind → 0, alone in its commit (row B23's own fix) · `91bb2945` R4 — a registered acceptance with no row in the ruler is itself red — and the ruler wired into `scripts/hooks/pre-commit`, proven on a real commit attempt to refuse a staged denial (exit 1) and then to pass the restored tree · `54be275d` the records class names its second ruler in his ruler table (`dxb-verify`) · `93a59c68` the session-start ruler · `11b952c3` the root cause: `.claude/hooks/spec-bootstrap.sh` clipped by LINES while STATE.md's lines are 1–3 KB paragraphs, so it produced 52,329 bytes, the harness refused it and every session opened the file by hand; now cut by BYTES at a sentence boundary, **7,756 bytes, ruler 4/4**, and a fresh headless session (`66d92e72`) gave the four-line position with zero file reads. **Measured for him the same evening:** the start-up load is 67,068 tokens (the session log's own counter) — harness and ~150 tool schemas 30,370 · 133-skill listing 7,776 · `MEMORY.md` 4,471 · project `CLAUDE.md` 3,105 · claude-mem 1,700 · the position hook 677 delivered of 13,954 produced; and ten plugins called ZERO times in 400 sessions over 30 days cost 4,648 tokens at every start — **not one was disabled, his order of 2026-08-27 keeps them on.** Battery on the day: `pnpm construction:battery` BATTERY_RED with four pre-existing reds, each owned by its own row and none touched here — B36 `seed-is-fiction` (6) · C42 NEXT pointer · B36 `live-drills` (6) · B23 (closed by `3beb0295`). ═══** <!-- OPEN: B43 --> <br>**THE SEPTEMBER RULINGS THAT AMENDED THE DOCTRINE ABOVE — written IN PLACE above on 2026-09-15 (W3, LAW A, audit F006), so the doctrine now reads true without this block; kept as the dated index of his words and the ledger ids:** (a) step ④'s "never text-to-video from nothing" and "a shot generated from a prompt is scrap by policy" are amended: the road comes from the brief — "with a prompt" (T2V) or "with a storyboard / pictures" (I2V) or "choose the best"; the general default is T2V and I2V is not forbidden; a human or product enters as a real photograph OR a written sheet <!-- CEO-OK: t2v-i2v-expert-choice-2026-09-03 --> <!-- CEO-OK: road-comes-from-the-brief-t2v-default-2026-09-04 -->. (b) "Voice from TTS" is cancelled: the engine's own voice is the voice, measured by WER against the script <!-- CEO-OK: tts-cancelled-engine-voice-only-2026-09-04 -->. (c) Every generated face is born inside MiniMax H3 from text (AHMET DXB-A-010, JAMES DXB-A-011; their references are frames of their own take); no Flux face and no Flux frame is handed to the local video engine — scoped by his words of 2026-09-14 and made precise the same afternoon <!-- CEO-OK: flux-local-engine-only-everything-made-here-2026-09-14 -->: *"Yerelde: MiniMax her şeyi baştan sona yapar; Flux kullanılmaz. Dışarıda: Üretimde Flux'tan faydalanılabilir. T2V ve I2V: İkisi de sistemde bulunur"* and, on the author's question, (A) — *"sadece minimax h3 iş yaptığı zaman flux'a ihtiyaç yok. bunun dışında dışarıda yapılacak işler için kullanılabilir bir kısıtlama yok. ama içeride kesinlikle öncelik yerel motor minimax begining to end"*; and his correction of the record's words: everything of a piece — script, storyboard, panels, stills, first frames, the cut — is made HERE on this computer on either route, only the ENGINE that shoots the take differs (the "off the station" wording was wrong — *"bilgisayar dışında ne ya, belki dışarıda api ile oluşturacağımız vitrinin herşeyini biz burada üreteceğiz"*); the local engine is the first choice, beginning to end; a take shot by an external engine (RunPod, an API or an MCP hand) may be handed a Flux still or first frame made here, without restriction beyond the brief's road; text-to-video and image-to-video are both open from the start on either route (EYW-002's Flux-frame trial on the station failed identity 0.27–0.50; his 2026-09-04 17:05 *"hepsini MiniMax'e yaptır, resim verme"*; C68); the four Flux-drawn presenters are out of use <!-- CEO-OK: ahmet-cast-member-born-in-engine-2026-09-04 --> <!-- CEO-OK: flux-avatars-retired-and-complaint-numbering-2026-09-13 -->. (d) Steps ⑤–⑥: LAW D — everything is made and judged at the engine's native draft (640×1152 vertical / 864×480 horizontal) first; nothing is upscaled before his eye accepts the draft; 1080 is the ceiling he chose for UGC, 2K is enough, no 4K test <!-- CEO-OK: law-d-draft-first-upscale-last-2026-09-03 --> <!-- CEO-OK: engine-standard-4-steps-no-upscale-unless-asked-2026-09-04 -->. (e) The engine standard is 4 sampling steps (a 15 s take ≈ 10.5 min on this card; 8 steps is too slow for him). (f) The holding has no brand restriction of its own — a third-party mark appears as it is in the real picture; the engine still never draws lettering, a readable mark comes from the real file, laid in post <!-- CEO-OK: no-brand-restriction-2026-09-03 -->. (g) The cast is MEN and ELDERLY WOMEN only; Elif and Nora retired, codes kept <!-- CEO-OK: avatar-cast-men-and-elderly-women-only-2026-09-03 -->; his addition of 2026-09-15 <!-- CEO-OK: cast-law-client-may-order-female-content-2026-09-15 -->: the holding's OWN cast stays so, but if a CLIENT asks for an advertisement with female-presenter content it is produced — the responsibility is the client's (written into the casting seats in W5). (h) The creative brain is Claude Fable 5.1 at effort xhigh (not max), Opus 5 the disabled standby; no persona file carries a model name <!-- CEO-OK: studio-brain-fable-5-1-opus-5-standby-2026-09-05 --> <!-- CEO-OK: creative-brain-effort-xhigh-2026-09-03 -->. (i) Measured corrections of 2026-09-01 on this card: "steps 6–9 need no card" is FALSE here (RealESRGAN ×4 ran 2.09 s per frame, 37 % of a film's clock); every cut restarts the engine (+37 % card per finished second on an 8-shot film against one take); a finished second costs 2–5 minutes of this machine. (j) SeedVR2 is the finishing step, measured 2026-09-03: 3B → 1080-class 4.07–4.25 s/frame (≈ 24.5 min per 15 s); 3B → 2K 7.5 s/frame; 7B-sharp → 2K 5.64 s/frame — faster than 3B at 2K and faithful to the face where 3B redraws it (`.planning/research/study-cards/seedvr2-topaz-equivalent.md`, `/home/dxb/tools/h3/upscale/results/`). (k) The reviewers of a take see frames, not video, and three seats wrote "unverified by ear" on 005 — leg (4)'s listening hand. (l) 2026-09-15, his word on the brains <!-- CEO-OK: studio-brains-open-set-defaults-switchable-2026-09-15 -->: no restriction to Fable 5.1 / Opus 5 — GPT Solo 5.6, GPT Astra 6 or another model may serve; the director, the screenwriter and every creative seat default to the smartest model of the day (today Fable 5.1), the other seats to Opus 5; any seat's brain switchable at any moment by him or by Hamza with one click, and a new model addable inside the studio; noted as B08 step (7) — a to-do, not built. <br>**WORKING PRACTICE BORN ON THIS ROW (board intent, NOT CEO laws or standing rules — his ruling 2026-09-15 <!-- CEO-OK: board-rule-like-sentences-are-not-ceo-laws-2026-09-15 -->: a board sentence becomes a rule only with his separate word; none of these carries one; their stories are in the diary; audit F018):** when the CEO names a folder, a file or a path, it is opened and LOOKED AT — images included — before any other candidate is considered (2026-09-01: his UGC storyboard in `~/Downloads/` was never opened and the wrong film was shot) · every product carries a code `DXB-<TÜR>-<MÜŞTERİ>-<SIRA>`, issued once, kept when rejected; the code is a FIELD on job, scene and shot when the studio screen is built (`~/tools/h3/studio/KATALOG.md`) · the DXB Stüdyo Vitrini (`~/tools/h3/studio/index.html`, port 8899) is TEMPORARY, a simple reference for what this row's screen shows and never a specification of it · a studio job is born under an active project or the pre-gate refuses it · no skin-mark descriptor in a casting brief, ever · a film folder holds videos, audio and stills only (the post scripts delete their frames) · a deletion he orders is executed only after the per-folder list WITH sizes is in front of him · the brief phrase "a phone on a tripod" draws the phone in frame. <br>**BUILT AND STANDING — the ledger id beside each says WHICH it is: ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE, or BUILT ON HIS ORDER and not yet looked at (LAW B), or CLOSED BY HIS WORD** (heading corrected 2026-09-15, W2, audit F004: plan approvals and a delegation are consents to build, not acceptances): the department `media-studio` — ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE — 16 seats (14 written in person + 2 held by assignment), gated, bound — **but the 2 assigned seats (Prompt / Model Specialist, Editor) CANNOT take a studio task today: their home profiles (`design.mcp.json`, `marketing.mcp.json`) carry 0 `media_*` tools and `queue_create_task` / `queue_dispatch` refuse a seat from another department (measured 2026-09-15; audit F033) — the studio runs 14 on the road; the assignment he approved 2026-09-03 has its record only in persona text; the remedy was planned as W9 (drawer grant per employee + the dispatcher accepting an assigned seat, registered as an A19 adaptation) — **F033 closed 2026-09-15 on his "onay", ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE the same day** <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-15 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w9-assigned-seats-plan-approved-2026-09-15 -->: `agent_assignments` carries the two rows the 2026-09-03 founding ordered (seat, media-studio, title, since 2026-09-03, the ledger id) on both engines; `dxb-mcp/media` granted `grantee_kind='employee'` to the two seats through `control_library_action`; the compiler gives each an overlay = its HOME kit + exactly the five `media_*` tools (23 → 28, nothing else added, nothing removed) while `design.mcp.json` and `marketing.mcp.json` still emit **0** — nobody else gained a hand; both dispatcher doors accept an assigned seat through ONE implementation and refuse a stranger unchanged. Road proof kept on the construction engine (`scripts/b43/w9-road-proof.mjs`, sheet `DXB-W9-ROAD-PROOF`): the Editor, home `marketing`, holds a `queued` task in `media-studio`; a re-run returns the same sheet, no second crew. **The studio now runs 16 on the road.** The company engine was SELECT-only in this part. Evidence `EVIDENCE-W9-2026-09-15.md`**; **F009 closed 2026-09-15 on his word "kaldır", ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE the same day** <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-15 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w7-voice-hand-removed-2026-09-15 --> — W7, road (a) of the two he was given (remove outright / gate to his order). The cancelled TTS hand is gone: `voice` left the `media_jobs` kind CHECK on BOTH engines (migration 20260915003000, the constraint recreated `NOT VALID` so the door shuts without validating — and therefore without endangering — the rows already written), left `media_submit`'s params, description entry and enum, and the lane's runner with its `ENGINES` key; **0** references to the TTS binary remain in the repo's source (2 before). The five historical `kind='voice'` rows are DELIBERATELY KEPT — 5, all `done`, ids-md5 `9ffe4755…` identical before and after; removing them is W12 and needs his separate word, because closing a door is not a licence to burn the logbook. The holding's own SPEAKING voice was measured untouched rather than promised untouched: `packages/voice` 0 lines changed, `voice_identities` fingerprint `2ae50c4c…` unchanged, Hamza still `speaches:piper / tr_TR-fahrettin-medium / active`, `voice_calls` 102. Evidence `EVIDENCE-W7-2026-09-15.md`; **F022 closed · F023 closed · F026 closed · F047 closed · F049 closed — 2026-09-15, W8, on his word *"V8'e başla"*, ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE the same day** <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b08-step0-w9-w7-w8-accepted-2026-09-