re-split into 4–6; hard cuts, no crossfade in the exam; every endpoint gated before it propagates; two seeds per design. The first plan's "Flux still" was withdrawn — Flux plays no part in a take the local engine (MiniMax H3) shoots (his rulings of 2026-09-04; C68 opened on his words) — **scoped by his word of 2026-09-14 to the local route only:** *"flux kareleri sadece bu bilgisayardaki localdeki model için kapalı. diğer runpod veya api veya mcp için değil. çünkü burada yani localde üretim yaptığımızda herşeyi baştan sonra minimax H3 yapıyor. ok."* — on a rented card, an API or an MCP hand a drawn frame is not closed (the four Flux-drawn presenters stay out of use as recorded 2026-09-13; his word did not reopen them). DONE on that word, and then CORRECTED THE SAME DAY ON HIS ORDER <!-- CEO-OK: continuity-rule-contradictions-removed-2026-09-14 -->: the first pass had only ADDED the rule and left the old doctrine standing beside it (the Creative Director's "six to ten perfect short shots", the Film Director's "six to ten … beat one thirty-second take every time", the still lane's "first and last frames handed to the motion lane", the Editor's "six to ten short generated shots", the product seat's "approved still as the first frame"); he caught it (*"Yeni kuralı yazmışsın ama eski zıt talimatları bırakmışsın … Yalnız yeni cümleyi ekleyip eski emri bırakma"*) and approved the correction (*"Bu düzeltmeyi yapmanı onaylıyorum"*). The sweep covered every seat that applies the road — 12 persona files (10 studio seats + the Prompt / Model Specialist and the Editor held by assignment), 44 sentences replaced; then each seat's prompt was rendered through the runtime loader (`@dxb/voice` `loadPersonaBody`) and the HR compiler (`compilePersonaPrompt`, full and compact) — the FIRST render found 6 of the 12 seats still without the rule in their own words or with an old phrasing left (12/24), so the rule was written into those six in the seat's own terms and two phrasings re-worded;