e Film Director's founding "a close-up holds identity for about three seconds … a scene longer than the hold time is several shots, never one" — superseded by the measured one-take 15 s films; the Creative Director's "a six-second shot cut into a thirty-second film beats one thirty-second generation"; the storyboard's "what the engine receives is already the film"; the product seat's "a real photograph in a perfect still"; the Advertising Director's "close-ups planned as separate shots, never asked of one long generation"; the Prompt / Model Specialist's 2026-09-03 "strong default" clause, out of date since his 2026-09-04 22:35 word; the Failure Analysis seat's "the cause is the long single take"), and the road's rule stated in the seat's own terms where a seat lacked it (storyboard, engineer, continuity, screenwriter, editor). The check was rebuilt as a wording check (several wordings per condition plus a contradiction list) — the "20/32 → 32/32" of that hour was a scratch script outside the repo, the kept test had 28 phrase checks and compiled through a path the runtime never calls (found by the evening audit; rebuilt again on the executor's own path — WHERE THIS ROW STANDS, evening); old-phrase sweep 0/16; every changed file re-submitted, gated, bound and verified 16/16; LIVE_BOUND_MATCH 16/16; tests r31 + b43 + b39 71/71; seats' status untouched. The check lives on as `tests/b43/road-consistency.test.ts`. **The same afternoon, his three sentences and his correction of the record's words (amendment (c) above):** the place words "on the station's own road / off the station" — in the 13 seat files that carried them (the other three had none) — replaced by engine words ("for a local-engine take (MiniMax H3 on this card)" / "for an external engine's take"), his canonical sentence written into all 12 applying seats (everything made here on this computer; only the engine that shoots differs; the local engine first, beginning to end; Flux plays no part in a local take; no restriction for an external engine's take; T2V and I2V both open from the start), condition 4 of the test grown to it and the place words made contradictions; delivered, verified 16/16, LIVE_BOUND_MATCH 16/16, the battery green (numbers in the evidence file). **Instruction corrected; not yet tried in production** — the first exam is the first job that needs more than one take; this is not an approval to make a film or start a paid service. Evidence `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/EVIDENCE-continuity-rule-2026-09-14.md`; no code. **(4) THE QC LIST ON THE ROAD — understanding report and plan first, his approval, then code:** its first item was never open — the ruling of 2026-09-03 (the engine never draws lettering) already answers what an engine-drawn mark on a prop is, and the product seat did not apply it to 004's take while 005's verdict did; its second item is a listening hand (the engine's voice against the written lines; three seats wrote "unverified by ear"); wardrobe, flow, object state and a calibrated identity threshold follow. **(5) THE EXTERNAL AUDIT when he brings the auditor** <!-- CEO-OK: external-audit-before-next-leg-2026-09-03 --> — the evidence files above, claim by claim. **(6) THE EXTERNAL HANDS READY — written on his order of 2026-09-14 (*"yapılacak birşey varsa tahtaya yaz sonra vakti geldiğinde yapılsın"*), built when its time comes, after an understanding report, a plan and his approval (Phase 2):** <!-- CEO-OK: external-hands-ready-leg-2026-09-14 --> his doctrine, in his words the same day: the studio has several routes — *"bizde bir kaç yol olacak higgfield onlardan biri, veya minimax h3 API veya başkası. en iyileri en mantıklıları seçilip kullanıma hazır hale entegre edilmeli seçim vakti gelince işe göre duruma göre yapılır"* — and the monthly membership is a running cost of the studio while the holding has advertising work, covering the whole month's production across every job, **never charged to one job or one film** (*"ben bir iş için sadece 59 euro vermeycem"*). READY means three things: each route is one hand in the studio's `media` tool group (`media_submit` with the route as data), its price per finished second in the cost table the CEO reads before the job (his order of 2026-08-31); its key in the vault, never in the repo; and the route passed once with the same brief as the station (the exam) before it is offered. Money out per route (a membership, a prepaid balance) is his approval, one proposal each (B41). **Measured 2026-09-14, the candidates (prices ex-VAT, vendor pages read live; blind-vote Elo from Artificial Analysis, text-to-video with audio / image-to-video; every number and source in `.planning/quick/20260903-media-studio-founding/EVIDENCE-external-hands-2026-09-14.md`):** ① **Higgsfield Plus over its official MCP** (`mcp.higgsfield.ai`; €47/month billed annually · €59 monthly; 1,200 credits/month, reset monthly (⚠ UNVERIFIED — two third-party sources, the vendor FAQ not read); the "unlimited" models are web-only — every MCP generation deducts credits; Start & End Frame control and image reference on Kling Omni 3): the breadth route — 30+ engines behind one hand; a 15 s ad costs Kling 3.0 1080p 24 credits (≈ 50 ads/month), Kling Omni 3 FLF 18 (≈ 66), Hailuo 2.3 1080p 30 (≈ 40), Wan 3.0 1080p 52.5 (≈ 22), Veo 3.1 1080p 116 (≈ 10), Seedance 2.0 1080p 135 (≈ 8 — the Plus pool is 2.2 minutes of Seedance 1080p a month, so Seedance and Veo there are hero-shot seconds, not volume). Elo: Kling 3.0 1080p 1,108 / 1,077 · Veo 3.1 1,089 / 1,089 · Seedance 2.0 1,220 / 1,197 · Wan 3.0 1,242 / 1,178; Higgsfield's "Hailuo 2.3" is the previous, silent, closed MiniMax generation, not H3. ② **MiniMax H3 on MiniMax's own API** (pay-as-you-go, no membership; 768p $0.08/s · 2K $0.13/s; audio included; the first five reference images free; T2V and Ref2V the same price; not in their prepaid packs yet): the station's own engine family at full size — 15 s = $1.20 / $1.95; Elo 1,226 / 1,190, above Kling and Veo. ③ **fal H3 Max** (MiniMax H3 open weights post-trained by fal on fal's own inference engine, ~35× the official endpoint's throughput; endorsed by MiniMax's H3 team): list price from 2026-09-15 768p $0.08/s · 1080p $0.16/s, Turbo half of that; the 75 %-off launch price ends 2026-09-14; **five generations a day free** for a signed-in account, up to 15 s each — the exam on this route costs nothing; T2V and I2V the same price; audio included; Elo 1,231 / 1,206 (#1 image-to-video with audio). **The author's reading, not a ruling:** for the hero shot the H3 routes (② or ③) are the measured best in price × quality and carry the station's recipes unchanged; Higgsfield is the breadth route for volume and for the engines the station will never hold (Kling, Veo, Seedance); the station stays the free road for everything that needs no more. Not started; nothing integrated; the code of the hands still knows one route (measured 2026-09-14: `media.ts` 311 lines, `media-lanes.ts` 113, `dispatch-book.ts` 430 — RunPod 0, Higgsfield 0, API 0 mentions). <br>**F057 closed · F058 closed · F059 closed · F060 closed · F061 closed · F062 closed · F065 closed — 2026-09-15, W13, on his word *"başla"*, ACCEPTED BY HIS EYE 2026-09-16 (LAW B).** <!-- CEO-OK: studio-b43-road-accepted-by-his-eye-2026-09-16 --> <!-- CEO-OK: w13-studio-contract-registered-2026-09-15 --> The studio was founded on 2026-09-03 and ran twelve days owned by no spec: measured 2026-09-15, word-bounded, DATA_MODEL · EVENT_MODEL · COST_CONTROL · APPROVAL_ENGINE · OBSERVABILITY · WORKFLOW_ENGINE and 00-INDEX carried **0** mentions of it, and the four clock/QA tokens **0** files in the whole corpus outside this board. **Registration only — nothing was built** (guard: no file under `db/` `packages/` `apps/` `tests/` `scripts/` in the commit; migrations 169/169/169; `media_jobs` triggers 0; `approval_rules` 8; `workflows` 0). **F057** DATA_MODEL now carries the job book as it really is — 20 columns, 32 rows