: `docker exec -i supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS psql -U postgres -d postgres -At -c "select lane, rule, active from media_routing order by lane"` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L03 --> **(03) THE RUNPOD LANE — the rented machine for when our own card is full or the job is too big** — owner: the AUTHOR session for the lane; the CEO for the rent, because renting is money OUT · finding: F073 · deliverable: a second lane beside our own station: when the card is busy or the job exceeds it, the shot is shot on a rented RunPod machine, and he sees the rent as a figure before it is spent and as a cost row after · accept: one shot runs from start to finish on a rented machine and its euro cost lands in that job's cost rows; the lane stands SWITCHED OFF by default and only his word switches it on, because it spends money outward · proves: `bash scripts/b43/runpod-lane-check.sh` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L04 --> **(04) THE ENGINE x MACHINE MEASUREMENT — what one second of film costs on each engine and each machine** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the bench measurements feed it · finding: F073 · deliverable: a measured grid — every engine down one side, every machine across the top (our own card, each rented size) — each cell saying how long one second of finished film takes there and what that second costs in euro · accept: not one cell is an estimate: each names the run it was measured from, and a cell nobody has measured yet reads 'not measured' rather than a number somebody imagined · proves: `node scripts/b43/engine-machine-matrix.mjs --verify` · status: planned · gate: his word · <!-- W14-L05 --> **(05) THE VISIBLE DIAL — he turns quality up or cost down, and sees the price BEFORE he commits** — owner: the AUTHOR session; the dial's drawing is gated on B32 like every studio screen · finding: F073 · deliverable: a dial on his own screen that he turns with his hand — quality one way, cost the other — with the price of THIS job standing beside it