25 **The plan, over that table.** (1) **Hamza**, chat and voice, gets Claude's own tools and skills and the holding's plugins — the first half of his V2 rule (2), "he has hands" (board §2d, 2026-08-01). The second half — he delegates from the conversation and the send-as-a-task button disappears — stays with that ruling and is not this leg. (2) **The classifier, the decomposer and the QA judge** are unchanged. (3) **Employees** keep the company's own tools and gain Claude's own tools, skills and the plugins. (4) **Every outside hand installed for the holding goes to every department**, so all 22 can research. (5) **The approval gate is unchanged**: money out, contracts, ad spend and identity steps still stop at him (doctrine §1 item 7). Everything loads only when needed (`ToolSearch`). Built-ins, skills and plugins enter the record as library items with a grant for every department, so doctrine §1 item 4 (the record chain) still holds.
27 **Wall 2 — everyone at its own desk.** The company works and writes only under its own home (`company-claude`); the repository and the construction's `~/.claude` are write-denied; the construction's secrets (`~/.claude/.credentials.json`, the repository's `.env*`) are read-denied. The plugins are copied onto the company's desk and loaded from there (`plugins: [{type:'local', path}]`) — **except claude-mem**: his 2026-08-27 words above, *"orada farklı bir beyin ve hafıza sistemi olacak"*; the company keeps its own memory drawer.
