   119	
   120	**LAW A — a live CEO order DELETES what contradicts it** (CEO, 2026-07-30). Not a footnote
   121	beside it, not "superseded but retained". The contradicting text goes, and the report says
   122	what went. Keeping both is how a record starts lying.
   123	
   124	**LAW B — finished ≠ approved** (CEO, 2026-07-30): *"iş tamamlanınca bitti anlamına gelmez,
   125	ben bakmam lazım."* A green battery means the AUTHOR's work is done. Only the CEO's own eye
   126	makes something **accepted**. No record may say approved / accepted / onaylandı / kabul
   127	edildi without an entry in `scripts/governance/ceo-approvals.json` carrying his words and
   128	the date. The battery fails on an unregistered approval claim.
   129	
   130	## 2. The boundaries that never bend
   131	
   132	- **The approval gate.** Money OUT, contracts, ad spend, identity steps and the subjects he
   133	  marks stop at the CEO. Money IN and routine outward communication do not.
   134	- **Ask before any project work.** Nothing in the project starts until he has said so in this
   135	  conversation (CEO 2026-10-01).
   136	- **Do not state as fact what you did not check.** Owner: `00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-MEASURE-NEVER-GUESS.md`.
   137	- **Evidence before done.** A completion claim cites the command and its decisive output. Anything a terminal cannot observe is labelled `⚠ UNVERIFIED — requires
   138	  human-eye confirmation` and listed apart. Door: `dxb-verify`.
   139	- **A fix must not break what stands around it; the tests show it.** Door: `dxb-verify`.
   140	- **Islamic boundaries are constitutional.** CEO-only. Code may refuse its own work against
   141	  them and warns him once; his word after that warning is done once as an exception, the boundary unchanged
   142	  <!-- CEO-OK: b64-q3-decision17-covers-everything-2026-10-14 -->; code may never widen or narrow them.
   143	- **Code: the session writes it; inside `dxb-team2` a fork, a `helper-writer` and the `builder`
   195	  audit shows wrong is corrected by the builder in its own `records(ruler): …` commit, never inside the
   196	  build commit it measures <!-- CEO-OK: audit-law-checker-only-checks-2026-09-15 -->.
   197	- **Dispute:** the lead runs the evidence Sol gave — it fails → real, fixed; it holds → the finding drops
   198	  and the report says why. A question no test can settle is the lead's, with its reason in the report.
   199	- **Sol unavailable** (quota, error, timeout): on an ordinary job the `refuter` subagent (Opus 5.5 ·
   200	  `high`) audits once, and the report says *"audited by Opus instead of Sol — read-only by word, not by
   201	  tool — because …"*; on money, a database or security the lead waits for Sol's window and works on
   202	  something else. No job closes unaudited; the auditor is never swapped silently
   203	  <!-- CEO-OK: fallback-auditor-named-and-refuter-second-round-gone-2026-10-04 -->.
   204	
   205	## 5. Tests
   206	
   207	- New behaviour is proven by a test written first — red before the code, green after. A test that can
   208	  never go red — one that recomputes its expected value the way the code does — is a defect.
   209	- After each piece, its own tests. After Sol's fixes, the touched tests again.
   210	- **Code changed → `pnpm typecheck`, then the battery, before Sol** — Sol reads its output instead of
   211	  marking it unverified, and reads the engine only after the battery has stopped writing to it
   212	  <!-- CEO-OK: dxb-team2-overall-look-fixes-2026-10-06 -->; again after the fixes when a fix changed code;
   213	  and a resident service whose
   214	  code changed is restarted (`dxb-verify`). The typecheck covers `packages/` and `apps/`, then `tests/` and
   215	  `db/seed/` (`tsconfig.tests.json`, since 2026-10-06). The battery: `pnpm construction:battery`, the whole suite in
   216	  both halves against the construction's own engine (port 54422), 1,486 tests, about 6 minutes
   217	  (2026-10-04). Launch it detached from a shell whose `oom_score_adj` is 100; green is the line
   218	  `BATTERY_GREEN`. It answers the one question no single test can: did this break anything else.
   219	- **Text only** → no battery. A door, the core or a record: the commit hook's rulers read those on
   220	  every commit. A persona's words: `bash scripts/persona-ruler.sh` (dxb-verify), which the commit
   221	  hook does not run.
   222	- The commit hook runs by itself on every commit: the secret scan (gitleaks); the records ruler when
   223	  STATE, the board or the ledger change; the opening ruler when the core, a skill or the opening hook
   224	  change; the research ruler and `tests/b46` when the research engine changes.
