Neither plan yet meets the brief end to end. A has stronger coverage, retrieval, and real-job validation; B has clearer packaging checks and a tested-only employee release. Both still leave gaps in bounded browsing, composition checks, and the approval path.

The registry compiler also ignores version and content when resolving grants: it passes the item’s name to the runtime. B’s dated bundle therefore needs an explicit install and version check; the database tag alone cannot pin what an employee loads.
